{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/542004-pathfinder-mythic-solars-playtest-actually-playable","id":542004,"title":"Pathfinder: Mythic Solars Playtest, actually playable","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-05T19:33:25-07:00","id":542004,"title":"Pathfinder: Mythic Solars Playtest, actually playable","content":"<b>(Part 1)<br /> <br /> (I forgot to mention this in the title but PEACH)<br /> <br /> Solar Exaltation</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The moment when a character gains her first Mythic Tier is called her Exaltation. This is similar to Mythic Ascension for a character with a Mythic Path, and indeed Mythic Paths, Exaltation and Mythic Ranks are mutually exclusive. Exalted characters, for all rules purposes, are considered Mythic characters.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Solar\u2019s Exaltation (which can refer both to the moment she received her power and the resilient spark of divine power that rests within her) is granted to her directly by the Unconquered Sun, the highest amongst the Celestial Incarnae and King of the Gods. The Unconquered Sun has a finite number of these Exaltations; a mere 150 Solars to defend all of Creation, and as such is extremely selective about those who receive His power. Mortals can receive Solar Exaltation only if they are at least 3rd level and levels in NPC classes do not count toward this minimum.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>The following are universal abilities all Solars gain as they increase in Tier. They gain these abilities in addition to any abilities from their specific Caste. Unless otherwise stated, they work exactly like their base Mythic Ability equivalents, see <i>Mythic Adventures </i>page 12.</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"4\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Base (Casteless) Solar Abilities</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Mythic Tier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Ability Score</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Mythic Feat</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Base Exalted Abilities</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Hard To Kill, Essence Pools, Anima Banner, Surge +1d6, Limit</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Amazing initiative</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Recuperation</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Surge +1d8</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Mythic Saving Throws</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Force of Will</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Surge +1d10</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Unstoppable</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Legendary Hero, Surge +1d12</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Ability Score:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Upon reaching the 2nd Mythic Tier, an ability score of your choice permanently increases by 2. At 4th, 6th, 8th, and 10th Tiers, another ability score of your choice permanently increases by 2; this can be an ability score you've already increased or a different ability score.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mythic Feat: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Select one Mythic feat or non-Mythic feat as a bonus feat. You must qualify for this feat normally. You gain another mythic feat at 3rd Tier, and again every 2 Tiers thereafter.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Personal Essence Pool (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Exalted characters can draw upon a wellspring of power to accomplish amazing deeds and cheat fate. This power is used by a number of different abilities. Each day, you can expend \u201cmotes\u201d of Personal Essence equal to 3 + double your Mythic Tier (5/day at 1st Tier, 7/day at 2nd, etc.). This amount is your maximum amount of Personal Essence. If an ability allows you to regain motes of Personal Essence, you can never have more than this amount.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Peripheral Essence Pool (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In addition to your Personal Essence pool, you also gain a second pool of Essence called your Peripheral Essence pool. This pool functions much the same as the Personal Essence pool except as follows. Each day, you can expend motes of Peripheral Essence equal to 6 + six times your Tier (12/day at 1st Tier, 18/day at 2nd, etc.). This is your maximum amount of Peripheral Essence. If an ability allows you to regain motes Peripheral Essence, you can never have more than this amount. When an effect causes you to regain a certain number of motes, they are not allocated to your Peripheral Essence pool until your Personal Essence pool is full.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>Sidebar: Mythic Power vs Motes: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Uses of Mythic Power and motes of Essence are, essentially, the same resource measured in a different metric. If an Exalt gains an ability (such as a Mythic Feat) or an item that requires her to spend Mythic Power, she can instead spend triple that amount in motes for the same effect. If an effect would normally increase an Exalt\u2019s maximum amount of Mythic Power, that Exalt instead increases her maximum personal Essence pool by 1 and her maximum peripheral Essence pool by 2 for every use of mythic power the effect would normally grant.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Likewise, a Mythic creature may gain an ability that requires that creature to spend motes of Essence. This means the creature may, at some point, have one or more thirds of a use of mythic power. It may be easier to keep track of that character\u2019s mythic power as motes from that point on, even if the creature doesn\u2019t actually use motes. Alternatively, you could keep track of fractional Mythic power gained in this way as a repeating decimal, fraction, or mixed number.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Anima Banner (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When you spend uses of Peripheral Essence a bit of the power leaks into your Anima; an invisible aura possessed by all living creatures. This leak creates a visible phenomenon called an Anima Banner. This banner grows more intense as you spend more Essence, but this intensity decreases by one step for every minute your character doesn\u2019t spend any Peripheral Essence.</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Solar Anima Banner Intensities</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Motes Spent</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Effect</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">The character\u2019s Caste Mark begins to shine faintly on the character\u2019s forehead and continues to visibly shine even at higher Anima banner intensities. This mark counts as a Holy Symbol of the Unconquered Sun the character is actively presenting.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">As above, additionally the character\u2019s Caste Mark shines as a candle, providing dim light for 5 feet.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">As above, additionally, the character is surrounded by a corona of light as bright as a <i>light</i> spell-like ability<i>,</i> providing normal light for 20 feet and dim light for 40 feet.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">13</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">As above, additionally the character\u2019s Anima Banner functions as a <i>daylight </i>spell-like ability, providing normal lighting for 60 feet and dim light for 120 feet.</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">19+</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">As above, additionally the character\u2019s Anima Banner continues to function as a <i>daylight</i> spell-like ability, but provides normal lighting for 120 feet and dim light for 240 feet. At this level the Anima also shapes itself into some symbol or image known as the Exalt\u2019s Totemic Display. Unlike other intensities, the Totemic Display fades to the 13-mote level after a single round rather than a minute.</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Hard to Kill (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Whenever you're below 0 hit points, you automatically stabilize without needing to attempt a Constitution check. If you have an ability that allows you to act while below 0 hit points, you still lose hit points for taking actions, as specified by that ability. Bleed damage still causes you to lose hit points when below 0 hit points. In addition, you don't die until your total number of negative hit points is equal to or greater than double your Constitution score.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Surge (Su):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> You can call upon your Essence to overcome difficult challenges. You can expend three motes to increase any d20 roll you just made by rolling 1d6 and adding it to the result. Using this ability is an immediate action taken after the result of the original roll is revealed. This can change the outcome of the roll. The bonus die gained by using this ability increases to 1d8 at 4th Tier, 1d10 at 7th Tier, and 1d12 at 10th Tier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Limit (Su):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Whenever you successfully save against a compulsion effect or are forced to act egregiously out of alignment, you gain a point of Limit, to a maximum of 10. Once you reach 10 Limit, you lose all your Limit points and suffer the effects of a Limit Break from the list of Solar Limit Breaks. You get a Will save to establish partial control of yourself (DC 15 plus your Tier), as detailed in that Limit Break\u2019s description.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Amazing Initiative (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At 2nd Tier, you gain a bonus on initiative checks equal to your Mythic Tier. In addition, as a free action on your turn, you can expend three motes to take an additional standard action during that turn. This additional standard action can't be used to cast a spell. You can't gain an extra action in this way more than once per round.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Recuperation (Su)</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: At 3rd Tier, you are restored to full hit points after 8 hours of rest so long as you aren't dead. In addition, by Expending three motes and resting for 1 hour, you regain a number of hit points equal to half your full hit points (up to a maximum of your full hit points) and regain the use of any class features that are limited to a certain number of uses per day (such as barbarian rage, bardic performance, spells per day, and so on). This rest is treated as 8 hours of sleep for such abilities. This rest doesn't let you regain motes or any Exalted or Mythic abilities that are limited to a number of times per day.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mythic Saving Throws (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At 5th Tier, whenever you succeed at a saving throw against a spell or special ability, you suffer no effects as long as that ability didn't come from a mythic source (such as a creature with a mythic Tier, mythic ranks or an Exalt). If you fail a saving throw that results from a mythic source, you take the full effects as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Force of Will (Su)</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: At 7th Tier, you can exert your will to force events to unfold as you would like. As an immediate action, you can expend three motes to reroll a d20 roll you just made, or force any non-mythic creature to reroll a d20 roll it just made. You can use this ability after the results are revealed. Whoever rerolls a roll must take the result of the second roll, even if it is lower.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable (Su)</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: At 8th Tier, you can Expend three motes as a free action to immediately end any one of the following conditions currently affecting you: bleed, blind, confused, cowering, dazed, dazzled, deafened, entangled, exhausted, fascinated, fatigued, frightened, nauseated, panicked, paralyzed, shaken, sickened, staggered, or stunned. All other conditions and effects remain, even those resulting from the same spell or effect that caused the selected condition. You can use this ability at the start of your turn even if a condition would prevent you from acting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Legendary Hero (Su): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">At 10th Tier, you have reached the height of Exalted power. You regain motes at a rate of 3 per hour, in addition to regaining your full pool after resting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gaining Tiers</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A character's knowledge and growth as an Exalt is classified by Tier, with a 1st-Tier Exalt already being significantly more powerful than an un-Exalted character of the same level and a 10th-Tier Exalt having power equal to that of the greatest of the gods. Mythic Tiers are similar to levels in a class or prestige class in that the powers gained at each Tier are added to all those that came before, but Tiers are gained in a different manner from levels. A character gains a new Mythic Tier by completing a number of trials that occur during play. A trial is a difficult task that adds to the legend and story of your character. Achieving a new Mythic Tier occurs independently of Experience point progression (though you will also gain Experience points for the various encounters you complete as you progress through your trials).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Trials are moments in the story when you must rise above the deeds of lesser heroes. These moments become critical junctures in your legend. The GM decides what qualifies as a trial, and it's up to you to complete it as you would other adventures. You might not even know you are attempting a trial until it is completed and the GM informs you to note it on your character sheet, though you'll likely get an inkling when you find yourself facing a particularly challenging foe or attempting something that most would find impossible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The number of trials required to attain each new Tier appears on Table: Trials per Tier. For Example, suppose a 5th-level fighter receives Exaltation and becomes a 1st-Tier Dawn Caste. Over a number of sessions, she earns enough Experience points to gain her 6th level of fighter. During this time, she doesn't complete a trial, so she doesn't advance to the next Dawn Caste Tier. During the next session, however, she engages in a climactic battle against a Fair Folk warlord that has been ruthlessly pillaging the countryside for slaves with a hobgoblin army; by defeating the Fae, she completes her trial, allowing her to become a 2nd-Tier Dawn Caste. To reach 3rd Tier, she will need to accomplish two more trials. A Solar can't gain more than 10 Tiers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Note that the number of trials needed to achieve the next Tier might vary from the number listed on Table: Trials per Tier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The GM can reduce or increase this number as needed to suit the campaign\u2014refer to the Mythic Trials section of </span></span></span><i>Mythic Adventures </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">for more guidance.</span></span></span> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Trials Per Tier</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup>*</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">-</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*The first Tier is gained at the moment of Exaltation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Path Abilities as Dominion Abilities: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Note that some Dominion Abilities function like analogous Mythic Path Abilities. These abilities mechanically identical but the Tier requirements use the Tier requirements of the Dominion Ability, not the associated Path Ability.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Solar Limit Breaks</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Note that some Limit Breaks can be dispelled early by magic such as </span></span></span><i>calm emotions </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">or </span></span></span><i>remove curse, </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">as detailed in their descriptions. Using magic to end a Limit Break early requires a DC 35 caster level check, and failure means the spell has no effect on the Exalt whatsoever. Anyone who attempts to magically end a Limit Break early is contesting Neverborn-level sorcery, after all.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Limit Breaks and the Great Curse are not known qualities of Solar Exaltation, so any use of these spells on Solars in Limit Break needs to be spontaneous to avoid metagaming. For example, a spellcaster might think to cast </span></span></span><i>calm emotions</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> on an enraged Solar just as he might any suddenly, inexplicably furious ally.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Mage\u2019s disjunction</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and </span></span></span><i>remove curse</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> are always valid choices for this method, even if the Limit Break description in question does not specify any magic that can dispel it. Additionally, </span></span></span><i>mage\u2019s disjunction</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> has a 5% chance to work in spite of a failed caster level check.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Trying to avoid dispelling a Limit Break directly by simply assuming magical control over the Exalt in question (such as with </span></span></span><i>dominate monster </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">or </span></span></span><i>geas)</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> still requires the caster level check above, and does not end the Limit Break early, even if you are able to </span></span></span><i>force</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> them not to comply with its conditions for the duration. If allowed a save, a Solar in Limit Break will always choose to do so against such magic, and rolls any such saves with a +10 profane bonus.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The simplest magical means to deal with a Solar in Limit Break may be to just incapacitate them. Solars under Limit Break do not gain any special defenses against spells like </span></span></span><i>deep slumber, hold person</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> or a good old fashion</span></span></span><i> horrid wilting.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Compassionate Martyrdom:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For one hour after reaching limit break, you are wholly directed by a need to alleviate the suffering of others in the most direct and dramatic manner possible. Upon seeing an overseer beating slaves, for example, you will stand before the whip before allowing someone other than yourself to suffer.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On a successful Will save, you must still directly and immediately aid those who are suffering, but can choose to do so more effectively. In the above example, you could simply kill the overseer and set the slaves free.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Tears:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For one hour after reaching limit break, the grief and suffering you have witnessed in the world overwhelms you, and you can do nothing but weep pitiably. You cannot function for the remaining hour, and only attempt to flee if attacked or endangered. If you are unable to flee, you can deal with the problem directly, but with a -2 penalty to all attack rolls, saving throws, ability checks and skill checks, as well as a -4 penalty to your initiative.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you pass your wills save you can defend yourself against danger normally but still take the penalties to rolls as listed above. You cannot be proactive or seek out danger or conflict, only react when it confronts you or your close allies in the vicinity directly.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Dispel:</b><i> calm emotions</i><br /> <br /> <b>Red Rage of Compassion:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You are enraged by the suffering you\u2019ve seen for half an hour after Limit Break, and immediately attack the closest obvious cause. You enter a rage, as per the barbarian class feature, with an effective barbarian level equal to twice your Tier. Your rage overcomes sense or reason. You are unlikely to even perform simple actions such as putting down what you are holding or drawing a weapon before simply attacking unarmed or with whatever you happen to be holding. If there is no great cause of suffering in the immediate area, you instead move around erratically, smashing objects with no regard to their value and attacking anyone foolish enough to interfere. A rage granted by this ability lasts the entire duration, but you are fatigued as normal afterwards.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On a successful will save, you must still immediately choose to attack a source of suffering, but can choose to do so effectively. You can choose whether or not to enter a rage like a barbarian, and may draw a weapon, or drop, say, the corpse of the unjustly slain peasant you were cradling in your arms a moment ago, if either action allows you to destroy the source of your rage more effectively.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Dispel: </b><i>calm emotions</i><br /> <br /> <b>Deliberate Cruelty:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You become unspeakably cruel in pursuit of your goals for one hour after Limit Break. You are incapable of empathy for the duration. If you perceive any other creature\u2019s weakness (real or imagined) interfering with your goals, you can only react with contempt. You will casually use torture, mutilation, and any other means at your disposal to instill fear and obedience. You suffer a -5 penalty to any Charisma-based check not related to fear or intimidation.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On a successful Will save, you can moderate your cruelty if necessary. You can show restraint and indifference when cruelty would obviously be less effective, and your penalty on social rolls decreases from -5 to -2 for the duration.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Heart of Flint:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You lose emotional capability all together for three hours after Limit Break. You don\u2019t quite become an automaton: you only consider efficiency when considering your next course of action. As a result, your speech becomes tactless, and you take a -5 penalty on Charisma-based checks for the duration.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As above, but you suffer a -2 penalty instead of a -5 penalty on Charisma-based checks for the duration. Your emotions are simply suppressed rather than lost. Your primary motivation is still efficiency, but you can avoid doing things you have a strong emotional aversion toward.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Dispel: </b><i>heroism</i><br /> <br /> <b>Ascetic Drive:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For one hour after Limit Break, you must seek simplicity or penance. You shave your head, clad yourself in rags, or otherwise dress simply. You begin removing items that increase your AC or improve your ability scores and leave them where they fall. You give all currency on your person to the closest individual that looks like they need it (though you can be persuaded to give it to an ally through roleplay), and retreat somewhere away from worldly concerns. You will not take any action to increase your level of physical comfort, or make small talk on trivial matters.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On a successful Will save, you act as above, but do not need to flee from the world or remove magic items You still cannot accept any luxuries such as sleeping indoors (unless it\u2019s very dangerous to do otherwise) or wearing anything but the most practical of clothes, such as armor. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Contempt of the Virtuous:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For one hour after limit break, any character flaws in other people disgust you, and you will do all within your power (including magic) to put them on the path toward righteousness. You are disdainful of anyone you\u2019ve previously witnessed overindulging or acting without honor. If you see anything even remotely self-indulgent or dishonorable, you attempt to intervene, physically if necessary. You self-righteously (and loudly) urge everyone around you to turn away from sin or weakness and adopt a more honorable lifestyle.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You must prevent your immediate companions and subordinates from committing unrighteous or dishonorable acts, but not others. You disdain strangers or superiors you see as sinful, but only lecture them if you believe they are trying to tempt you, or if they ask for your opinion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Overindulgence:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For one hour after limit break, you lose all sense of self control. You take to sex, drugs, alcohol and gluttony with equal vigor, and will not listen to reason or wait for a more appropriate moment for your debauchery. You indulge in all the vices available to you, regardless of expense or consequence. If you are unable to pay for these vices, you will attempt to borrow or steal until you can afford them.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can be persuaded into performing the bare minimum of what duty and obligation require of you; such as commanding an army or pursuing an enemy. With any time you can spare, however, you will indulge in any vices that are available to you in that instant. You can avoid drinking on duty, but not being exceptionally hung over. You will always say yes when directly offered a vice for free.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Dispel: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Any spell that grants a direct bonus to Will saving throws.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Berserk Anger:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For half an hour after Limit Break, you enter a rage, using twice your Tier as your effective barbarian level. Furthermore, if something moves, you </span></span></span><i>will</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> try to kill it. You start with obviously hostile creatures in your vicinity, but after they are dead, you move onto bystanders, and if you finish them off, your own companions. If you run out of creatures to attack, your surroundings draw your ire; you attempt to sunder or break any objects within reach as you look for more blood to spill. A rage granted by this Limit Break always lasts for the duration, and you are fatigued afterwards as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On a successful will save, you can avoid attacking allies (as long as they don\u2019t get in your way) and those you are committed or sworn to protect. Anyone else, however, remains a target. You also needn\u2019t attack inanimate objects and, in lieu of other targets, you can choose to move to an area where your anger will be productive.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Dispel: </b><i>calm emotions</i><br /> <br /> <b>Foolhardy Contempt:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You become senselessly courageous for two hours after Limit Break. You gain a +15 profane bonus on saves against fear. You always place yourself in the front lines of battle, challenge the most powerful-seeming enemy you can see to single combat, accept any and all dangerous missions, and will never retreat under any circumstances.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Partial control: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On a successful Will save, you are still without fear, but not without sense. You can retreat or avoid battle if tactically inadvisable. You still do not take personal risk into consideration when forming a plan, however. Your profane bonus on saving throws above is reduced from a +15 to a +5.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Dispel: </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Any magical fear effect, though you must fail your save, if applicable.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Universal Dominion Abilities:</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A Solar may select any one of these Dominion Abilities in lieu of gaining an out-of-Caste Dominion Ability.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Extra Mythic Feat (Ex): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You gain an extra mythic feat. You can take this ability a number of times equal to half your mythic tier (minimum 1). Each time you do, you gain another mythic feat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Legendary Item (Ex): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You gain a legendary item. This item grants a number of abilities equal to your tier (maximum 3). At 3rd tier, you can select this ability again, increasing the maximum to six abilities and causing the item to become a lesser artifact. At 6th tier, you can select this ability again, increasing the maximum to 10 abilities; the item then becomes a greater artifact.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Dawn Caste</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Dawn Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Tier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Terrifying Visage, Dawn Dominion Ability,</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Dawn Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Dawn Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Dawn Dominion Ability</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Bonus Hit Points: </b>Whenever you gain a Dawn Caste tier, you gain 5 bonus hit points. These hit points stack with themselves and don't affect your overall Hit Dice or other statistics<br /> <br /> <b>Terrifying Visage (Ex):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> When your Anima banner is at the 3</span></span></span><sup>rd</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> intensity or higher, you gain a bonus on your intimidate checks equal to your Tier. You may spend 3 motes as a swift action to make an intimidate check against all hostile creatures that can see you.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Dominion Ability:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Every Tier, you learn one Solar Dominion Ability. These Dominion Abilities can be from your own Caste or any other Solar Caste. Starting at the 1</span></span></span><sup>st</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier and every three Tiers thereafter (4</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, 7</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, and 10</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">) this Dominion Ability must be a Dawn Dominion Ability, or a mythic feat with a style feat as a prerequisite. Note that some Dominion Abilities are spell-like abilities, unless stated otherwise, these Dominion Abilities function at a Caster Level equal to twice your Tier. The Dawn Caste Dominions are Archery, War, Martial Arts, Melee, and Thrown.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Archery Dominion Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>There Is No Wind (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Far Shot (feat) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a standard action and by spending 4 motes, you make a single flawless ranged attack. You take no penalties from range to this attack roll (though you must still fire within your weapon\u2019s maximum range) gain </span></span></span><i>darkvision</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> up to your weapon\u2019s maximum range </span></span></span><i>before</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> selecting your target, and ignore concealment. You also ignore unfavorable winds and other kinds of natural weather that might negatively impact your shot. By spending two additional motes, you may ignore even supernatural wind and weather such as a </span></span></span><i>wind wall</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> spell. At 4</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier, you may spend two additional motes on this Dominion Ability and fire this shot at any target you can see, even one beyond your weapon\u2019s maximum range.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Accuracy Without Distance (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites:</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> There Is No Wind, Base Attack +2.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a free action, you may spend three motes and gain the benefits of the </span></span></span><i>true strike</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> spell on your next ranged attack.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Forceful Arrow (Sp):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">There Is No Wind </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 2 motes as a standard action you, make an attack with a ranged weapon and imbue your ammunition with a powerful force effect. If you hit a creature\u2019s touch AC they are immediately subject to a bull rush using your CMB. If you hit a creature\u2019s normal AC they are subject to the bull rush plus the normal damage from the ranged attack. At 6</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier you may select this ability again. If you do, you can use this ability as a ranged attack action instead of a standard action.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Trance of Unhesitating Speed (Su):</b><i>Prerequisites:</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Base attack +2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When you make a full-attack action, you can make up to half your Tier (minimum 1) in additional ranged attacks by spending 2 motes per attack. Each attack you make in this way has a cumulative -1 penalty to the attack roll (-1 for the first attack, -2 for the second, and so on).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Arrow Storm Technique (Su):</b><br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Trance of Unhesitating Speed, Base Attack +5, Tier 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a full round action and by spending 6 motes, you may make a ranged attack against a number of creatures or objects within range and line-of-sight equal to 4 + your Tier. Make one attack roll and compare it to the AC of all your targets, this attack hits every target with an AC equal to or lower than your attack roll. You must have separate ammunition equal to your number of targets (though you may use Phantom Arrow Technique, as normal). If this attack roll threatens a critical, it only threatens a critical on one target (your choice).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Essence Arrow Attack (Su):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Whenever you make an attack that uses ammunition, you can spend 2 motes to give your ammunition an enhancement bonus equal to your Tier, up to a maximum bonus of +5 (not including weapon qualities). You can apply any of the following weapon qualities to ammunition you enhance this way, </span></span></span><i>holy, flaming, axiomatic,</i><i>flaming burst, shocking, shocking burst, demon bane, devil bane, daemon bane, fey bane, magical beast bane, aberration bane, </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">or </span></span></span><i>undead bane.</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Adding these properties consumes an amount of the enhancement bonus equal to the property\u2019s base price modifier (see Table 15-9 on page 469 of the Core Rulebook). Unlike the normal rules for adding weapon qualities to ammunition, ammunition you enhance in this way does not need a minimum enhancement bonus of +1 before you start adding weapon qualities.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Phantom Arrow Technique (Sp):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Essence Arrow Attack</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Whenever you make an attack that uses ammunition, you can spend one mote per piece of ammunition you would normally need to fire a sparkling phantom version of your normal ammunition as a spell-like ability. This Dominion Ability can be used to create non-magical, mechanically-simple, thrown ammunition you are proficient with, even if you do not have any of that ammunition on hand. This Dominion Ability is a conjuration (creation) effect. Ammunition created by this Dominion Ability fades from existence after inflicting its damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Summoning the Loyal Weapon (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Phantom Arrow Technique or Call the Blade</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a move action, you can banish a weapon you are carrying and are proficient with to a special plane called Elsewhere for one mote. You can summon any weapon you\u2019ve banished in this way by spending one as a move action (or as part of a move action if you have a Base Attack Bonus of +1 or higher, or as a free action if you have the Quick Draw feat). Both of these powers are conjuration (summoning) effects. This is an Archery Dominion Ability if you use Phantom Arrow Technique as the prerequisite and a Melee Dominion Ability if you use Call the Blade as the prerequisite.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Immaculate Golden Bow (Sp):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Summoning the Loyal Weapon, Phantom Arrow Technique.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 3 motes as a move action, you conjure a golden composite bow of pure Essence with an appearance based on your personality or preference. Each time you use this Dominion Ability you choose either a short composite bow, or a long composite bow. This weapon has hit points equal to 4 + your Tier, hardness 10 + your Tier, and an enhancement bonus equal to half your Tier (minimum 1) and the </span></span></span><i>adaptive<sup>UC</sup></i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> weapon quality. This weapon fades from existence after a number of hours equal to your caster level. This Dominion Ability is a conjuration (creation) effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Rain of Feathered Death (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Manyshot, Phantom Arrow Technique, Arrow Storm Technique, 6</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 4 motes you increase the number of arrows you can fire with Manyshot on your next attack by 2 at sixth Tier and 3 at 9</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Melee Dominion Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hungry Tiger Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tier 1,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You know by how many degrees of 5 you exceeded your opponents AC by whenever you do so with a melee attack. Additionally, when you hit with a melee attack, you can spend two motes per five on your attack roll that exceeded your target\u2019s AC. For every 2 motes spent in this way, your attack does an extra 1d6 points of precision damage, which stacks with other sources of precision damage (such as Sneak Attack), up to a maximum of 1d6/Tier (plus all precision damage from other sources). Like other sources of precision damage, this damage is not multiplied on a critical hit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Fire and Stones Strike</b><b>(Ex):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hungry Tiger Technique or Falling Icicle Strike</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Regardless of the alien nature of your foe, you can always find a way to hit </span></span></span><i>something </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">important. You can choose to spend 3 motes whenever you successfully hit with an attack. If you do, that attack ignores Damage Reduction and affects creatures immune to precision damage as if they weren\u2019t immune to precision damage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Peony Blossom Attack (Ex):</b><i>Prerequisites:</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Base attack +2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When you make a full-attack action, you can make an additional number of melee attacks, up to half your Tier (minimum 1) in additional attacks by spending 2 motes per attack. Each additional attack you make in this way has a stacking -1 penalty to the attack roll (-1 for the 1</span></span></span><sup>st</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> attack, -2 for the 2</span></span></span><sup>nd</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, and so on).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Iron Whirlwind Attack (Ex):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Improved Two-Weapon Fighting (feat) or Whirlwind Attack (feat); 3</span></span></span><sup>rd</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You gain Fleet Warrior, as per the Champion Path Ability:</span></span></span><br /> <i>Fleet Warrior (Ex): </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When making a full attack, you can move up to your speed either before or after your attacks. This movement provokes attacks of opportunity as normal.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>One Weapon, Two Blows (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Base attack +6, Tier 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can spend 3 motes whenever you make a full attack, your attack bonus on the additional attacks you gain by having a high base attack bonus is 5 higher. This ability can\u2019t give any of these attacks a higher attack bonus than your total attack bonus for the initial attack. For Example, a 12</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> level fighter with an attack bonus of +16/+11/+6 would have, with this ability, an attack bonus of +16/+16/+11. This ability doesn\u2019t reduce the penalties from two-weapon fighting, improved two-weapon fighting, greater two-weapon fighting, or other situational penalties on attack roll (such as Combat Expertise, Power Attack, fighting defensively, or harmful conditions). You can select this ability more than once. Each time you select it, the attack bonus on additional attacks increases by another 5, to a maximum of your highest attack bonus, meaning a 12</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> level fighter above with two purchases of this ability has an effective attack bonus of +16/+16/+16.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Invincible Fury of the Dawn (Su):</b><i>Prerequisites:</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Whirlwind Attack (feat) or Improved Two-Weapon Fighting (feat); 6</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When you make a full attack action, you may spend 4 motes to gain your surge die on all your attack rolls that turn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Call the Blade (Sp): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Base Attack +2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending one mote as an immediate action in response to a disarm attempt. If you do, you gain a +3 circumstance bonus to your CMD against that combat maneuver check. As long as there is an unobstructed flight path between a weapon you own and yourself, you may spend one mote to have that weapon fly to your outstretched hand as a free action, at a movement rate of 60ft. Catching this weapon is also a free action. You may spend one mote to draw a weapon as a free action; the weapon telekinetically flies from its sheath, holster, or straps to your hand. All of these powers are transmutation effects.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Summoning the Loyal Weapon (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Phantom Arrow Technique or Call the Blade</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can banish a weapon you are carrying and are proficient with to a special plane called Elsewhere as a move action. You can summon any weapon you\u2019ve banished in this way by spending one mote as if readying a weapon normally (IE a move action, unless you have Quick Draw or a base attack bonus of +1 or higher). Both of these powers are conjuration (summoning) effects. This is an Archery Dominion Ability if you use Phantom Arrow Technique as the prerequisite and a Melee Dominion Ability if you use Call the Blade as the prerequisite.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Solar Saber (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Call the Blade</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 4 motes as a swift action, you conjure a golden sword of pure Essence with an appearance based on your personality or preference. Each time you use this Dominion Ability, you choose either a short sword, long sword, or scimitar, bastard sword, great sword, nodachi</span></span></span><sup>UC</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, wakizashi</span></span></span><sup>UC</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, or katana</span></span></span><sup>UC</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. This weapon has hit points equal to 7 + your Tier, hardness 10 + your Tier, an enhancement bonus equal to half Tier and the </span></span></span><i>holy</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> weapon quality. You can exchange this enhancement bonus for any of the following weapon qualities: </span></span></span><i>flaming, flaming burst, axiomatic, </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">or </span></span></span><i>keen.</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> This Dominion Ability is a conjuration (creation) effect. A sword conjured by this Dominion Ability fades from existence after a number of hours equal to your Tier. This Dominion Ability may be used to create a pair of short swords or wakizashi for a cost of two additional motes. Both weapons in this case are </span></span></span><i>holy</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> but the remainder of the enhancement bonus is split between the two.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Iron Raptor Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Call the Blade</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending one mote whenever you throw a melee weapon or thrown ranged weapon, you treat it as if it had the </span></span></span><i>throwing</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> and </span></span></span><i>returning</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> weapon qualities. Unlike a normal </span></span></span><i>throwing</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> weapon, this weapon\u2019s first range increment is equal to 20 feet + 10 feet per Tier, or its base range, whichever is higher.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Blazing Solar Bolt (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tier 6, Iron Raptor Technique</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As a standard action, you can cast holy solar fire from a melee weapon you are wielding for 4 motes. This is a ranged touch attack with a range of 50 feet + 5 feet per Tier you possess. If this attack hits it deals 1d10 + your strength modifier in damage, and an additional 1d6 points of damage per two caster levels. Half of this damage is fire damage, while the other half results directly from divine power (as per </span></span></span><i>flame strike)</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. Against undead, demons, and creatures with the evil subtype, this Dominion Ability inflicts 1d8 damage per two caster levels instead of 1d6 per two caster levels. This Dominion Ability is an evocation (fire) effect. A character can realize this Dominion Ability is similar to a </span></span></span><i>flame strike </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">spell with a DC 20 spellcraft check.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Bulwark Stance (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Base Attack +3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 3 motes as a swift action, you gain a +2 insight bonus to your AC and cannot be flanked until your next turn. This insight bonus increases by +2 for every 4 Tiers you possess beyond the 1</span></span></span><sup>st</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> (+4 at 5</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier, +6 at 9</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Heavenly Guardian Defense (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bulwark Stance.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you are not flat-footed and are wielding a melee weapon, you may spend 3 motes as an immediate action in response to an attack, before the attack roll is made. You block this attack with your supreme skill and Essence, gaining a +20 deflection bonus to your AC against that attack. When you use the parry class feature, you may spend 3 motes to automatically exceed your opponents attack roll by a threshold of one, and can parry any attack that has an attack roll (though you are still subject to splash damage as if you were hit indirectly if you parry a splash weapon in this way).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Fivefold Bulwark Stance (Su):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bulwark Stance, 6</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending up to 2 motes per tier as a swift action, you gain the benefits of Bulwark Stance for one round per 2 motes spent.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Solar Counterattack (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bulwark Stance, combat reflexes, Tier 3, Base Attack +6</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You may spend 2 motes in response to a melee attack made against you. If you do, that attack provokes an attack of opportunity from you.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ready in Eight Directions Stance (Ex):</b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Solar Counterattack, 6</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier,</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">base attack bonus +12</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You take a guarded stance and spend 5 motes as a standard action. If you do, melee attacks against you or your allies provoke attacks of opportunity from you until your next turn.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thrown Dominion Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>Joint-Wounding Attack (Ex):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> When you make an attack with a ranged weapon you can spend 2 motes. If you do, instead of rolling damage normally, you may instead elect to inflict 1d6 damage to a physical ability score of your choice. This Dominion Ability cannot reduce a target\u2019s constitution to 0.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Observer-Deceiving Attack (Su):</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> You can spend 3 motes when making a ranged attack to conceal the attack from observers. You attack appears to come from a different direction, reducing stealth check penalties from sniping by 10. Additionally, if you are using a small thrown weapon, such as a shuriken or throwing knife, creatures observing you must make a perception check (DC 15 plus half your Tier) to know you are making a ranged attack at all: creatures who fail do not notice you throw anything.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Falling Icicle Strike (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites:</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Observer-Deceiving Attack</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You know how many incriminates of 5 you\u2019ve exceeded your opponents AC by when you do so with a ranged attack. You can spend two motes per five on your attack roll that exceeded your target\u2019s AC. For every 2 motes spent in this way your attack does an Extra 1d6 points of precision damage, which stacks with other sources of precision damage (such as Sneak Attack), up to a maximum of 1d6/Tier (plus all other sources of precision damage). Like other sources of precision damage, this damage is not multiplied on a critical hit. You may ask the GM to inform you by how many degrees of five you exceeded your opponent\u2019s AC by before deciding to use this ability.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mists on Water Attack (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Observer-Deceiving Attack</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You may spend 3 motes when making a ranged attack to supernaturally silence your target. A creature hit by this ranged attack is affected by a </span></span></span><i>silence </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">spell, centered on its square, with no saving throws, but allowing spell resistance as normal. This effect can last a number of rounds equal to your Caster Level, but you must spend 3 motes for every round after the first to maintain it. This Dominion Ability is an Illusion effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>War Dominion Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>Rout-Stemming Gesture (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Charisma 12, Leadership (feat), Profession (Solider) 3 ranks.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 4 motes at any time during mass combat, or as a standard action outside of mass combat, you may steady the hearts of those who follow you. This Dominion Ability targets either 100 times your Tier scattered creatures you define, or an army you are attached to in mass combat. This Dominion Ability removes the shaken, frightened and panicked conditions immediately and makes the selected creatures immune to fear until your next action. A mass combat unit affected by this Dominion Ability automatically passes all Morale checks until the next tactics phase. Individuals or armies targeted by this Dominion Ability must be able to see or hear either you or a signal used by you they understand.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Commanding the Ideal Celestial Army (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Rout-Stemming Gesture, Profession (Solider) 4 ranks.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You spend 3 motes and, with a booming voice, prearranged signals or flawless relays, direct the forces under your command immediately. Friendly armies within 300 times your Tier feet receive a 12-word message instantaneously. You can use this Dominion Ability to give your Army Battlefield Advantage for one round if you, organized into a Fine army by yourself, would have Battlefield Advantage.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mob-Dispersing Rebuke (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Profession (Solider) 2 ranks</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You spend 5 motes and target a Large or smaller Army. That Army\u2019s commander must make a DC 14 Morale check or immediately route. At Tier 3 you may target a Huge or smaller army with this Dominion Ability. At 10</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Tier you may target a Colossal or smaller army with this Dominion Ability. This Dominion Ability treats disorganized rabble, protestors, mobs or other non-Army social units as Armies and can target them as above. Armies composed of creatures that cannot understand you are not valid targets for this Dominion Ability, but you may use a translator. You may choose to make this dominion ability a fear effect, but it is not by default.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Fury Inciting Presence (Sp): </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Profession (Solider) 2 ranks, Charisma 13</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 3 motes as a full round action, you incite your allies to righteous violence. Allies who can see and hear you benefit from a </span></span></span><i>rage</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> spell of the normal duration. This Dominion Ability can be used to incite greater strength and ferocity in an Army you are part of as well. As a free action during the Combat Phase, your army gains +2 OM but must use the Aggressive strategy until your next Tactics Phase.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>General of the All-Seeing Sun (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Fury Inciting Presence, Tier 3, Profession (Solider) 3 ranks</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By spending 3 motes, you are instinctually aware of the status of units under your command. You sense the current hit points, morale and strength of all friendly armies within ten times your Tier miles. For an additional mote, this Dominion Ability can treat individual allied creatures as Fine armies, allowing you to sense them with this Dominion Ability.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Heroism-Encouraging Presence (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Rout-Stemming Gesture, Fury Inciting Presence, Profession (Solider) 4 ranks</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Your example lends tremendous valor to those who fight with you. Whenever you use a spell, ability or feat that grants a morale bonus, you may spend two motes. If you do, all creatures benefiting from the moral bonus gain a +20 sacred bonus on saves against fear as long as they retain the morale bonus. This effect cannot be made permanent (such as with a </span></span></span><i>permanency</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> spell).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Tiger Warrior Training Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Heroism-Encouraging Presence. Profession (Soldier) 6 ranks. Tier 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can quickly turn even farmers and merchants into skilled, professional soldiers. With this Dominion Ability, you spend a number of weeks and can train and retrain a number of creatures equal to your Tier times 100 in the following ways:</span></span></span><br /> <i>Heroic Statline: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">NPCs with non-heroic statlines may gain heroic statlines of your choice after five weeks of your training.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Retrain PC Class Levels: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Characters with class levels in PC classes can Exchange those class levels for levels in any of the following classes: fighter, monk, paladin, antipaladin, cleric, warpriest, brawler, magus, ninja, rogue, bloodrager, slayer, barbarian, ranger, samurai or cavalier. This training takes 3 days per level retrained (Or 2 days per level retrained if the classes involved have retraining synergy; see </span></span></span><i>Ultimate Campaign</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> for more information on retraining).</span></span></span><br /> <i>Upgrade to PC class levels: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Characters with NPC class levels may exchange those levels for any of the PC class levels above by spending 5 days per level retrained. Such characters must have heroic statlines before benefiting from this training.</span></span></span><br /> <i>Train Tiger Warriors: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You may increase the character levels of creatures trained, up to a maximum of four. You cannot train creatures in this way beyond 4</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> level. Racial HD count as levels for the purposes of this cap. This training takes 10 days per level gained.</span></span></span><br /> <i>General Restrictions: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A creature with levels in a class greater than or equal to your own levels in that class cannot gain or retrain into any further levels in that class by way of this Dominion Ability. Tiger Warrior Training can only grant class levels in bloodrager, magus [eldritch scion] or a similar class if all the retraining NPCs have an appropriate magical lineage for that class or archetype.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Legendary Warrior Curriculum (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Tiger Warrior Training Technique, Tier 6, Profession (Soldier) 12 ranks.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This Dominion Ability enhances Tiger Warrior Training Technique. You can now train tiger warriors up to 7</span></span></span><sup>th</sup><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> level.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-06-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:43:26-07:00","id":542040,"title":"","content":"<b>(part 2)<br /> <br /> The Zenith Caste</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Zenith Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Tier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Repose, Midday Bulwark, Zenith Dominion Ability,</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Zenith Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Zenith Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Zenith Dominion Ability</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Bonus Hit Points: </b>Whenever you gain a Zenith Caste tier, you gain 5 bonus hit points. These hit points stack with themselves and don't affect your overall Hit Dice or other statistics.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Repose (Sp): </b>For a single mote as a move action, you can burn one corpse at close range (25 feet + 5 feet per caster level) (CL equals twice your Tier) with holy, golden fire. A normal corpse is destroyed by this ability and its soul passes on to an afterlife or reincarnation appropriate to the campaign setting. Neither the body nor the soul can be used to create an undead creature. If a corpse targeted by this ability is a component of an undead creature, that creature instead takes 1d6 damage per three caster levels. Half of this damage is fire damage, while the other half is direct divine energy (as per <i>flame strike</i>). A reflex save (DC equals 10 + your Tier + your Charisma or Wisdom modifier) halves this damage. This ability cannot burn a corpse with a size larger than colossal.<br /> <br /> <b>Midday Bulwark (Su): </b>At 1<sup>st</sup> Tier choose one of the following abilities:<br /> You gain DR/epic equal to your Tier against creatures with the evil or chaotic subtype.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Dominion Ability:</b> Every Tier, you learn one Solar Dominion Ability. These Dominion Abilities can be from your own Caste or any other Solar Caste. The Dominion Abilities you gain at the 1<sup>st</sup>, 4<sup>th</sup>, 7<sup>th</sup> and 10<sup>th</sup> Tiers must be a Zenith Dominion Abilities. Note that some Dominion Abilities are also spell-like abilities; unless stated otherwise, these Dominion Abilities function at a Caster Level equal to twice your Tier. The Zenith Caste Dominions are Integrity, Performance, Presence, Vitality and Nature.<br /> <br /> <b>Integrity Dominion Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>Integrity-Protecting Prana (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Wisdom 13<br /> You protect yourself from harmful transmutation by spending 7 motes as a standard action. For the next 24 hours, unwanted Transmutation effects that alter your mind, body or spirit automatically fail.<br /> <br /> <b>Righteous Lion Defense (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Iron Will<br /> Your commitment to your cause fills you with strength of will and bravery. Select a grand cause, relationship or ideal important to you. Whenever you roll a Will save against an effect that would cause you to betray that ideal, you gain +20 on that Will save. Intimidate checks made against you to betray that idea automatically fail, and you gain +15 on Sense Motive checks against deception that could undermine your faith in that ideal, or that, if believed, would lead you to unknowingly betray or hinder your cause. This Dominion Ability can be purchased a number of times equal to your Tier, each time it is purchased, select an additional cause, ideal or relationship.<br /> <br /> <b>Temptation-Resisting Stance (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Iron Will<br /> By spending 5 motes as a move action, you add half your Tier to your Will saves and sense motive checks for a number of hours equal to your Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Elusive Dream Defense (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Temptation-Resisting Stance<br /> Whenever you are called upon to roll a will save, you may spend 6 motes to gain a +20 to that save. Whenever you actively roll sense motive (not when the GM rolls secretly for you) you may spend 6 motes to gain +15 on your check.<br /> <br /> <b>Transcendent Hero\u2019s Meditation (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Improved Iron Will (Feat), Elusive Dream Defense<br /> By spending all your remaining motes (minimum 10) you immediately break all undesired enchantment or mind-affecting effects on yourself, even if you would normally be unwilling or unable to do so normally because of those effects. If you cannot pay the Essence cost for this Dominion Ability, you may instead take a number of d8s of slashing damage equal to your Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Sun King\u2019s Radiance: (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Charisma 15, Elusive Dream Defense<br /> While friendly creatures are aware of your presence, they gain your Charisma bonus to their intimidate DCs and as a bonus to their Will saves (this Charisma bonus stacks with a creature\u2019s own Charisma bonus if applicable; such as from a paladin\u2019s Divine Grace class feature).<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Maintaining Maneuver (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Wisdom 13<br /> Whenever you successfully pass a Will save against an enchantment effect, you may spend 3 motes as an immediate action and roll a Will save of an identical DC. If you pass, you gain no limit from resisting the enchantment effect.<br /> <br /> <b>The Performance Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Respect Commanding Attitude (Su): </b><br /> You may spend 3 motes to command the attention of those who watch or listen to your performance. Creatures that can see or hear your performance must make a Will save (DC 10 + your Tier + your Charisma modifier). If they fail, they must respectfully watch your performance, but they may make a new will save every 5 minutes. This Dominion Ability cannot be used on creatures that are aware of immediate danger or nearby combat. This is not a mind-affecting effect; your performance is simply exceptionally captivating.<br /> <br /> <b>Phantom-Conjuring Performance (Sp) </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Charisma 13, Perform (Any) 2 ranks.<br /> This with this Dominion Ability, you may use <i>major image </i>as a spell-like ability for three motes. You need either concentrate as normal to maintain this image or use it in conjunction with a performance without concentrating. In this case, the ability lasts as long as your performance + 3 additional rounds. Creatures gain a Will save to disbelieve this effect as normal (DC 13 + your Charisma modifier). You can give images and sounds conjured by this Dominion Ability vaguely ethereal or holographic appearances. If you do, creatures observing these sounds and images always know they are illusions, but you can activate this Dominion Ability without spending motes<br /> <br /> <b>Heart-Compelling Method (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Charisma 13, Perform (Any) 2 ranks,<br /> You may spend 5 motes to rouse emotions in others as part of a performance, using a Perform skill you possess. This performance lasts 10 minutes per three motes spent. Creatures who see or hear your performance may make a Will save (DC 10 + your Tier + your Charisma modifier) if they fail, they begin to feel an emotion you desire for the duration of your performance + one hour per two Tiers you possess (minimum 1 additional hour). While the specific emotion felt can be as detailed as you wish (Such as the sadness emotion specifically expressed as hopelessness), they all have one of the following mechanical effects:<br /> <i>Anger: </i>Affected creatures benefit from <i>rage</i>, as the spell.<br /> <i>Sadness: </i>Each affected creature takes a -2 penalty to initiative rolls, perception checks and Will saves.<br /> <i>Happiness/Confidence: </i>Affected creatures receive a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls, Will saves, and all skill checks other than perception and sense motive. On perception and sense motive checks, affected creatures take a -2 penalty instead.<br /> <i>Fear: </i>Creatures take a -2 penalty to saves against fear and increase their level of fear by one step.<br /> <i>Compassion: </i>Affected creatures gain a +2 morale bonus on heal, diplomacy, knowledge (religion) and Aid Another checks but take a -2 penalty to sense motive checks. Affected creatures also treat their caster levels for healing spells as one level higher.<br /> <i>Hate: </i>If you are Charisma 17 and inspiring anger at a specific group of creatures (as defined the favored enemy ranger class feature), you may inspire hate instead. Against that group, affected creatures gain a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls. Affected creatures also gain a +1 morale bonus on weapon damage rolls, Intimidate and Sense Motive checks against the targeted group.<br /> <br /> <b>Memory-Reweaving Discipline (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Perform (Oratory) 6 ranks, Phantom-Conjuring Performance, Heart-Compelling Method,<br /> As a standard action, you spend three motes and rewrite a number of creature\u2019s memory to see you as a trusted friend and ally. This Dominion Ability functions like <i>mass charm monster</i> except the Will save to negate the effect is DC 10 + your Tier + your charisma modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>Husband-Seducing Demon Dance (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heart-Compelling Method, Leadership (feat), Perform (any) 6 ranks, Tier 3.<br /> You are truly a god-king reborn. Your Leadership score improves by 2 and you always use your surge dice for free when attempting a call to action of some kind with a Perform, Diplomacy or other check at the GM\u2019s discretion.<br /> <br /> <b>The Presence Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Hypnotic Tongue Technique (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Diplomacy, Intimidate or Perform 6 ranks; 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier.<br /> You can spend 10 motes to cast <i>lesser geas </i>as a spell-like ability (Will save DC 14 + your Charisma modifier). At 6<sup>th</sup> Tier this spell-like ability can affect a creature regardless of its HD and its save DC increases to 10 + your Tier + your Charisma modifier.<br /> <br /> <b>Majestic Radiant Presence (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Charisma 13,<br /> You can spend 3 motes as a free action to emit an aura of incandescent radiance for a number of minutes equal to your Tier. Your Anima banner increases to the 8-mote level (or increases by one step, if already at the 8-mote level or higher) and creatures attempting to attack you must make a Will save (DC 8 + your tier + your Charisma modifier) if they fail, the attack against you fails. A creature need only make this save once per turn regardless of how many attacks it makes. This ability is a fear-effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrifying Apparition of Glory (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Intimidate 3 ranks, Majestic Radiant Presence<br /> When Majestic Radiant Presence is active, you can spend one additional mote as a free action to add your Tier to all intimidate checks. This effect lasts until your Majestic Radiant Presence ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Irresistible Salesman\u2019s Spirit (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Charisma 15, Diplomacy 3 ranks.<br /> You always add a competence bonus equal to your Tier to Diplomacy checks to improve a creature\u2019s attitude toward you.<br /> <br /> <b>Enemy-Castigating Solar Judgment: </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Charisma or Wisdom 13<br /> When you select this Dominion Ability you gain one of the following abilities.<br /> <i>Holy Strike (Su): </i>You may spend 2 motes any time you make an attack to give that attack the <i>holy</i> weapon quality and bypass the DR of creatures with the evil subtype.<br /> <i>Mythic Smite (Su): </i>This ability functions as the Champion Path Ability of the same name; as a free action, you can expend three motes to regain one use of your smite evil ability. For the rest of your turn, your successful attacks against evil creatures bypass all damage reduction. You must have the smite evil class feature to select this ability.<br /> You may select this Dominion Ability multiple times, but its effects do not stack; each time you take this Dominion Ability select a different ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Vitality Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Whirlwind Armor-Donning Prana (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Strength 13, Constitution 13, proficiency with the armor to be worn.<br /> This Dominion Ability allows you to complete a minute\u2019s worth of work equipping armor per mote spent as a full-round action. This is a transmutation effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Hauberk-Lightening Gesture (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites:</i> Whirlwind Armor-Donning Prana, proficiency with the armor to be stored.<br /> By spending one mote as a full-round action, you store armor you are wearing and have used in combat in a special plane called Elsewhere. You can summon that armor as a standard action at any time by spending one mote; the armor appears on your body equipped as it was when you stored it. This is a conjuration effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Glorious Solar Plate (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Hauberk-Lightening Gesture, Tier 3, proficiency with the armor to be conjured.<br /> By spending 4 motes as a standard action when you are not wearing armor, you conjure a suit of shining, golden armor forged from your Anima as a spell-like ability. You can conjure either scale mail, chain mail, steel lamellar, mountain-pattern armor, a breastplate, splint mail, banded mail, half plate, tatami-do, kusari gusoku, o-yoroi or full plate with an enhancement bonus equal to half your Tier. If you are not carrying a shield you may spend one additional mote to conjure a light or heavy shield, but the enhancement bonus is split between the armor and the shield. Items created by this Charm are fully equipped when you conjure them and always glow like a Solar anima at the 8-mote level. Items created by this charm have an aesthetic appearance based on your personality and preference, but are always unmistakably armor of the type conjured. This ability is a conjuration (creation) effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Armored Scout\u2019s Invigoration (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Hauberk-Lightening Gesture<br /> With this Dominion Ability you improve your armor\u2019s maximum dexterity bonus and decrease its check penalty by one point. This improvement increases by one point for every 2 Tiers beyond the first (+2 at 5<sup>th</sup> Tier, +3 at 7<sup>th</sup> Tier, and +4 at 10<sup>th</sup> Tier). Further, at 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier you no longer take a speed penalty for medium armor and at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier you no longer take a speed penalty for heavy armor.<br /> <br /> <b>Durability of Oak Meditation (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Constitution 15<br /> You can activate this Dominion Ability for three motes as an immediate action after being hit by an attack but before damage is rolled. If you do, you gain DR 10/epic against that attack. This stacks with a Zenith Caste Solar\u2019s Midday Bulwark Caste Feature.<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Kettle Body (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Durability of Oak Meditation<br /> You can suffuse your flesh with a golden force effect. This spell-like ability costs 1 mote and functions like <i>mage armor.</i><br /> <br /> <b>Adamant Skin Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Durability of Oak Meditation<br /> You may spend 4 motes as an immediate action in response to an attack, spell, area-of-effect or other external source of damage. You must choose to use this Dominion Ability before the attack roll is made, or, in case of an effect with a saving throw, before you roll your saving throw. You must be aware of the source of the incoming damage to use this ability. If you do, you negate all damage from that attack or effect, but are subject to (or required to save against) any non-damaging effects the attack or effect may have caused. (For example, if your AC is exceeded by 5 or more with a shield slam, you negate the damage from the attack but are still subject to a bull rush as normal.)<br /> <br /> <b>Battle Fury Focus: </b><i>Prerequisites:</i> Strength 13, Constitution 13<br /> Choose one of the following abilities when you gain this Dominion Ability:<br /> <i>Rage (Sp): </i>You can spend 2 motes to cast <i>rage</i> as a spell-like ability, but you may only cast it on yourself.<br /> <i>Mythic Rage (Su): </i>This works as per the Champion Path Ability of the same name: As a free action, you can expend one use of mythic power (three motes) to regain 1/4 your maximum number of rage rounds (minimum 4 rounds). For the rest of your turn, your successful attacks while raging bypass all damage reduction. You must have the rage class feature to select this ability.<br /> <br /> You can select this Dominion Ability more than once but its effects do not stack; each time you select this Dominion Ability, choose a different ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bloodthirsty Sword-Dancer Spirit (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Battle Fury Focus, Tier 3, Strength 15, Constitution 15<br /> Whenever you are raging or under the effects of a <i>rage</i> spell, you may spend 4 motes as an immediate action to improve your morale bonus to strength by +2 for the duration of the rage. At 7<sup>th</sup> Tier, your morale bonus increases by an additional +2. When you activate this Dominion Ability you gain DR 1/-. This DR increases by 1 for every 3 Tiers beyond the 3<sup>rd</sup> (DR 2/- at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier, DR 3/- at 9<sup>th</sup> Tier) and stacks with the barbarian damage reduction class feature and similar barbarian class features gained from archetypes at the GMs discretion (such as Invulnerability from the [Invulnerable Rager] archetype).<br /> <br /> <b>Unbreakable Warrior\u2019s Mastery (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Great Fortitude, Con 15<br /> Whenever you are subject to ability damage you can choose to activate this Dominion Ability as an immediate action. If you do, you take no ability damage; you instead loose a number of motes equal to the amount of ability damage you would have taken from the effect. Any damage over your number of remaining motes is taken normally. At 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier you can also use this Dominion Ability in response to level drain. If you do you lose seven times the number of levels to be drained in motes, but you take no negative levels. Any negative levels you are unable to pay motes to negate are applied normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Immunity to Everything Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Con 15, Great Fortitude<br /> This Dominion Ability prevents poisons and diseases currently affecting you from harming you for a number of hours equal to your Tier. You continue to roll saving throws against these diseases and poisons at the normal frequency, but there is no penalty for failure other than the disease or poison persisting. This Dominion Ability also immunizes you against any new diseases or poisons you are exposed to for the same duration; you can personally treat plague victims, spice your meat with rattlesnake venom or grapple with mummies without contracting any new ailments. This Dominion Ability applies to all poisons and diseases, including supernatural poisons and diseases, including mummy rot.<br /> <br /> <b>Body-Mending Meditation (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Con 15, Tier 3<br /> You gain Fast Healing, as per the Guardian Path Ability:<br /> <i>Fast Healing (Ex): </i>As a swift action, you can expend one use of mythic power to gain fast healing 5 for 1 minute. This ability can be taken a second time at 3rd tier or higher and a third time at 6th tier or higher. Each additional time you take this ability, the fast healing increases by 5.<br /> <br /> <b>The Nature Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Friendship with Animals Approach (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Handle Animal 2 ranks<br /> You can use <i>speak with animals </i>as a spell-like ability for 2 motes. While this ability is active, natural animals and vermin will not attack you unless significant pain or fear drives them to. Familiars, animal companions, bonded mounts and similar creatures may roll a Will save (DC 10 + your Tier + your Wisdom or Charisma modifier) to negate this effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Tied Pet (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Handle Animal 4 ranks, Animal Companion Class Feature<br /> You gain a Mythic Companion, similar to the Guardian Path Ability:<br /> <i>Mythic Companion (Su): </i>This works like the Guardian Path Ability of the same name but applies only to animal companions, bonded mounts and/or familiars. Select one animal companion, familiar, or bonded mount. That creature can use the surge ability a number of times per day equal to your Tier. Its surge ability uses the same bonus die type as you do when you use your surge ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Hardship-Surviving Mendicant Spirit (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Survival 3 ranks.<br /> For 6 motes you gain a +20 competence bonus on any survival check to find food and/or shelter. At 6<sup>th</sup> Tier you can use this ability at-will.<br /> <br /> <b>Element-Resisting Prana (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Survival 5 ranks.<br /> You can cast <i>resist energy </i>as a spell-like ability for 2 motes, but can only target yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>Trackless Region Navigation (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Survival, Profession (Sailor) Knowledge (Dungeoneering) or Knowledge (Geography) 3 ranks.<br /> You spend 6 motes gain a +20 competence bonus on a check for any skill you are trained in that is used to navigate. At GM\u2019s discretion this Dominion Ability\u2019s prerequisites could be met by another relevant skill based on the campaign setting.<br /> <br /> <b>Unshakeable Bloodhound Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Trackless Region Navigation, Survival 3 ranks<br /> You gain Supreme Tracker, as per the Guardian Path Ability:<br /> <i>Supreme Tracker (Su): </i>If you have something that carries a creature's scent (such as a personal item or piece of flesh), you can expend one use of mythic power (three motes) to create a supernatural bond that allows you track that individual.<br /> As a free action, you can sense the creature's general direction and distance, as well as know whether it is alive, dead, destroyed, dying, or undead. The creature must be on the same plane as you for this ability to function. For the purpose of spells and effects that block scrying and divination, your caster level for this effect is a number equal to double your Tier. At 6th tier, you can track the creature if it's on a different plane than you.<br /> <br /> <b>City-Moving Secrets (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 6, Survival 12 ranks<br /> By spending 10 motes a group you are leading no larger than your Tier times 1000 creatures gain the benefits of your Favored Terrains (if applicable) and gain a competence bonus on their survival rolls to find food and shelter equal to your Tier for a number of days equal to your Tier.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Twilight Caste</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Twilight Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Tier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Improved Mage Armor, Brilliant Improvised Spell, Twilight Dominion Ability,</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Twilight Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Twilight Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Twilight Dominion Ability</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Bonus Hit Points: </b>Whenever you gain a Twilight Caste tier, you gain 3 bonus hit points. These hit points stack with themselves and don't affect your overall Hit Dice or other statistics.<br /> <br /> <b>Improved Mage Armor (Sp):</b> If you have <i>mage armor</i> or <i>shield </i>in your spellbook, familiar, formula book or list of spells known, you may spend one mote to cast either spell as a spell-like ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Twilight Arcana (Su): </b>You can cast any spell of a spell level you can cast on your class spell list for 3 motes. Spells cast in this way count your caster level as two higher for caster level dependent effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Dominion Ability:</b> Every Tier, you learn one Solar Dominion Ability or Supernatural Martial Arts Technique. These Dominion Abilities can be from your own Caste or any other Solar Caste. Starting at the 1<sup>st</sup> Tier and every three Tiers thereafter (4<sup>th</sup>, 7<sup>th</sup>, and 10<sup>th</sup>) this Dominion Ability must be a Twilight Dominion Ability. Note that some Dominion Abilities are spell-like abilities, unless stated otherwise these Dominion Abilities function at a Caster Level equal to twice your Tier. The Twilight Dominions are Artifice, Insight, Knowledge, Healing, and Magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Path Abilities as Dominion Abilities: </b>Note that some Dominion Abilities function like analogous Mythic Path Abilities. These abilities mechanically identical but the Tier requirements use the Tier requirements of the Dominion Ability, not the associated Path Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>The Artifice Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Object-Strengthening Touch (Su)</b>: <i>Prerequisites: </i>Craft (any) 3 ranks.<br /> You can spend 3 motes and touch an object as a standard action to increase that object\u2019s Break DC and Hardness by 5 for one hour per Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Chaos-Resistance Preparation (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Object-Strengthening Touch<br /> By spending 5 motes as a standard action, you grant an object Spell Resistance equal to 10 plus your Tier and a bonus on saves equal to your Tier. These bonuses only apply against Chaotic spells and spell-like abilities, creatures with the Chaotic subtype, and any detrimental Transmutation effects that target the object. These bonuses last for one hour per Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Crack-Mending Technique (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Craft (any) 6 ranks.<br /> You can cast <i>make whole</i> as a spell-like ability for 2 motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Shattering Grasp (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Craft (any) 3 ranks.<br /> You spend 2 motes to add half your ranks in a relevant craft as an insight bonus to damage against objects and constructs was strength checks to break objects for one turn. The Craft skill you use for this ability is the same as the Craft skill you\u2019d normally use to create an object or construct of that type.<br /> <br /> <b>Craftsman Needs No Tools (Su): </b>Craft (any) 3 ranks.<br /> You may spend four motes whenever you begin a period of work on a crafting or spellcraft project. If you do, count as having proper, Masterwork (if applicable) tools for the project you are attempting as long as those tools cost less than 1000gp/Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence-Forged Wonders Understanding (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Spellcraft 6 ranks, Craftsman Needs No Tools, Craft Wondrous Item (Feat)<br /> When creating a magic item, you can spend motes equal to that item\u2019s Caster Level to halve the GP cost of the raw materials; you substitute some of the magical components you need with your own Essence instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder-Forging Genius (Su): </b>Prerequisites: Tier 6, Craft (any) 12 ranks, Essence-Forged Wonders Understanding, Crack-Mending Technique, Craftsman Needs No Tools<br /> Half your Tier always stacks with any Caster Levels you possess and skills you are trained in for the purposes of meeting the Caster Level and minimum skill ranks needed to create magic items (maximum 20). You always add your Tier as an enhancement bonus to Craft and Spellcraft checks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Insight Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Crafty Observation Method (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Perception 3 ranks<br /> You may spend 5 motes to complete the equivalent of 15 minutes of searching an area as a standard action. If you would normally need to disturb a scene (such as opening drawers, searching through papers or rummaging through cabinets) to find something, you do not need to so when using this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Soul-Discerning Method (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Sense Motive 3 ranks<br /> You can cast <i>detect chaos/law/good/evil</i> as spell-like abilities for one mote per casting.<br /> <br /> <b>Judge\u2019s Ear Technique (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Sense Motive 3 ranks.<br /> You can cast <i>discern lies</i> as a spell-like ability for 3 motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Irresistible Questioning Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Diplomacy or Intimidate 3 ranks.<br /> After spending 6 minutes interrogating a creature you can spend 4 motes to compel the creature to answer your questions honestly. A creature can resist this effect with a Will save (DC 10 plus your tier plus your Charisma modifier) but you are aware when this happens. Repeated use of this ability on a creature within 24 hours gives that creature a stacking +2 morale bonus to the associated Will save.<br /> <br /> <b>Courtier\u2019s Eye Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (Nobility) or Sense Motive 3 ranks.<br /> You spend 3 motes as an immediate action to gain an intuitive understanding of the social position of a creature you can see. If the creature in question is deliberately concealing its social standing you must defeat its Bluff check with a Sense Motive check, though you gain a bonus on this roll equal to your Tier. This Charm lets you know how many Class Levels the target creature has in aristocrat, cavalier, samurai, Noble Scion or a similar class at GM discretion. You can also discern how many Class Levels the character has in a class that is more common among the nobility of the region (such as wizard levels in a mageocracy) though this may require a Knowledge (nobility) roll on your part. In either case, you detect these levels as \u201caristocratic Class Levels\u201d rather than levels of a specific class. You also know how important the creature considers itself compared to other creatures you can see and how important those creatures think the target creature is compared to themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Consumer-Evaluating Glance (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Sense Motive 3 ranks<br /> You can spend 2 motes to roll Sense Motive after socially interacting with a creature. If you beat that creature\u2019s Bluff check, the GM or the creature\u2019s player must declare that creature\u2019s intentions for this interaction.<br /> <br /> <b>Harmonious Academic Methodology (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Intelligence or Wisdom 13, Tier 3<br /> You can quickly turn even the most illiterate brutes into thoughtful intellectuals and mages. With this Dominion Ability, you spend a number of weeks and can train and retrain a number of creatures equal to your Tier times 100 in the following ways:<br /> <i>Heroic Statline: </i>NPCs with non-heroic statlines may gain heroic statlines of your choice after five weeks of your training.<br /> <i>Retrain PC Class Levels: </i>Characters with class levels in PC classes can Exchange those class levels for levels in any of the following classes: cleric, magus, wizard, sorcerer, arcanist, bard, alchemist or investigator. This training takes 3 days per level retrained (Or 2 days per level retrained if the classes involved have retraining synergy; see <i>Ultimate Campaign</i> for more information on retraining).<br /> <i>Upgrade to PC class levels: </i>Characters with NPC class levels may Exchange those levels for any of the PC class levels above by spending 5 days per level retrained. Such characters must have heroic statlines before benefiting from this training.<br /> <i>Train Harmonious Scholars: </i>You may increase the character levels of creatures trained, up to a maximum of four. You cannot train creatures in this way beyond 4<sup>th</sup> level. Racial HD count as levels for the purposes of this cap. This training takes 10 days per level gained.<br /> <i>General Restrictions: </i>A creature with levels in a class greater than or equal to your own levels in that class cannot gain or retrain into any further levels in that class by way of this Dominion Ability. Harmonious Academic Methodology does not allow humanoids in Creation or a setting with similar restrictions to cast arcane spells without the requisite feats or traits.<br /> <br /> <b>Legendary Scholar Curriculum (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Harmonious Academic Methodology, Tier 6,<br /> This Dominion Ability enhances Harmonious Academic Methodology. You can now train Harmonious Scholars up to 7<sup>th</sup> level.<br /> <br /> <b>Chaos-Repelling Pattern (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Knowledge (Arcana) 4 ranks, Knowledge (the Planes) 4 ranks<br /> You can cast <i>magic circle against chaos </i>as a spell-like ability for 5 motes, but the radius equals your Tier times 5 feet (minimum 10 feet) and is always centered on you, even if and when you move. Additionally, when you cast <i>magic circle against chaos</i>, your anima flares briefly and seeps into the circle\u2019s edges. The area affected by a <i>magic circle against chaos</i> you cast always has Planar Traits like the Material Plane, regardless of what plane you are in at the time. Pervasive, harmful Planar Energy effects (such as Wyld Mutation) do not penetrate inside of a <i>magic circle against chaos </i>you cast. You can enhance a <i>magic circle against chaos</i> cast by another creature by imbuing it with your anima as a standard action for one mote.<br /> <br /> <b>Wyld-Shaping Technique (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Knowledge (Arcana) 6 ranks, Knowledge (the Planes) 6 ranks, Chaos-Repelling Pattern<br /> This ability permanently turns areas tainted by the Wyld (or other, chaotic planar energies at GM discretion) into stable parts of the Material Plane, in a process that requires four hours of dedicated concentration. You stabilize an area of the Wyld no greater than 10 10-foot squares per Caster Level. In the Bordermarches and Middlemarches, this ability returns these area as close as possible to its original state before the Wyld changed it (though it doesn\u2019t resurrect creatures killed by that change and does not reverse any natural aging creatures or objects in the area experienced.) In the Deep Wyld and Pure Chaos, this ability allows you to shape the new area as you see fit, as if using a <i>create demiplane</i> spell. If you choose to use the same Planar Traits as the Material Plane when stabilizing this area, the area counts as part of the Material Plane. If you assign any other Planar Traits to this area it counts as a demiplane you created with a spell such as <i>create demiplane,</i> though it is permanent (as per <i>permanency)</i> barring physical destruction, and unlike other demiplanes it is usually possible to simply walk to it from the Material Plane. To activate this ability you either spend 15 motes or expend a spell slot you can cast <i>create demiplane </i>with (if you cast spontaneously, you must know this spell. If you prepare spells, you must use a spell slot prepared with this spell.)<br /> <br /> <b>Wyld Cauldron Technology (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 4, Knowledge (Arcana) 8 ranks, Knowledge (the Planes) 8 ranks, Wyld-Shaping Technique<br /> Choosing to use this ability modifies Wyld-Shaping Technique. It converts areas of the Wyld (or areas tainted with other Chaotic planar energies, at GM discretion) at a rate of 20 10-foot squares per caster level and acts like <i>create greater demiplane </i>in the Deep Wyld or Pure Chaos. You can use this ability by spending 15 motes as normal, but if you wish to trigger this enhanced Wyld-Shaping Technique with a spell, you must use a spell slot you can cast <i>create greater demiplane</i> with instead.<br /> In addition, you may create people to populate this new land. You can create up to 1d8 humans per caster level when you use this ability in addition to its other effects. These people are always humans with 2 levels in an NPC class each. They recognize you as their creator and have the same alignment as you, but are not obligated to obey you.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence-Lending Method (Su): </b>You give some of your Essence to a touched Mythic creature as a standard action. You can give (your Tier times 3) motes to a creature with a single use of this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Power-Awarding Prana (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 4, Knowledge (Arcana) 8 ranks, Essence-Lending Method<br /> By spending 10 motes, a touched non-Mythic creature gains uses of Mythic Power per day equal to half your Tier, counts as a Rank 1 Mythic creature for the purposes of spells and abilities, gains a number of Mythic feats it meets the prerequisites for equal to half your Tier, and can use the Surge ability at one die type lower than your own. You can grant these powers to a number of creatures no greater than half your Tier at any one time. This template (the Solar Disciple template) adds +2 to a creature\u2019s CR at 4<sup>th</sup> Tier and +3 to a creature\u2019s CR at 7<sup>th</sup> Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Order-Affirming Blow (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 4, Knowledge (Arcana) 8 ranks, Wyld-Shaping Technique, Essence-Lending Method<br /> By spending 6 motes and making an unarmed strike or melee touch attack as a standard action or as part of a charge or bull rush, you purge a target of corruption. The target is subject to <i>break enchantment </i>and <i>remove curse</i> and any Chaotic effects or undesirable transmutation effects on the target are removed immediately.<br /> This ability treats creatures with the Chaotic subtype as if they were Chaotic effects themselves. Such creatures take 2d6 slashing damage per caster level. This damage ignores DR, but an effected creature is allowed a Will save (DC 10 + your Tier + your choice of your Intelligence, Charisma, or Wisdom modifier) for half damage. Fey creatures slain by this ability turn into statues, dreams, objects, animals or ordinary humans at GM discretion (if it is relevant, these humans are initially unconscious for 3d10 minutes and may have hazy memories of their previous lives, but generally wish to simply live as humans from now on).<br /> <br /> <b>Immanent Solar Glory (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Knowledge (Arcana) 6 ranks<br /> Your Personal Essence Pool increases by 2 and your Peripheral Essence Pool increases by 4. You can select this ability up to three times.<br /> <br /> <b>The Healing Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Touch of Blissful Release (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 2 ranks,<br /> By spending 7 motes and touching a creature as a standard action (or melee touch attack, if the creature resists you) you subject that creature to a <i>calm emotions </i>spell (unwilling creatures may make a Will save, DC 10 + your Tier + the higher of your Wisdom or Charisma modifiers). In addition to the effects of <i>calm emotions, </i>the effected creature does not feel pain for the duration of the ability. Touch of Blissful Release has a duration of one hour per caster level, rather than concentration, and the effect ends immediately if any other creature performs a hostile action against the effected creature, as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Contagation-Curing Touch (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 2 ranks,<br /> You can spend 3 motes when you make a heal check to perform that check as if you had (400gp + 100gp per Tier) worth of medical tools or medicines of your choice, and ignoring any penalties for unfavorable conditions such as poor sanitation or distraction. When using a spell that heals hit point damage, removes negative levels, heals ability damage, or restores the dead to life, you may ignore up to (400gp + 100gp per Tier) of the spell\u2019s material component cost by spending 3 motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Wound-Mending Care Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 2 ranks<br /> You may spend 3 motes when you make a successful heal check to restore hit point or ability damage. If you do, you always heal the maximum amount possible for that check. You may also spend 3 motes to empower any spell you cast to heal ability or hit point damage, as if using the empowered spell metamagic feat. If you have an ability that always empowers your healing spells (such as the Healer\u2019s Blessing domain power) a spell effected by this ability is maximized instead (as if using the Maximize Spell metamagic feat).<br /> <br /> <b>Wound-Cleansing Meditation (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 3 ranks<br /> You can spend two motes to cast <i>lesser restoration</i> as a spell-like ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Diagnosis Technique (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 2 ranks<br /> You can spend 1 mote to cast <i>diagnose disease </i>as a spell-like ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Ailment-Rectifying Method (Sp): </b><i>Prerequistes: </i>Heal 3 ranks, Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> You can spend 3 motes to cast <i>remove disease</i> as a spell-like ability. When you cast <i>remove disease, </i>you always gain a bonus on your caster level check to remove the disease equal to your tier. You may substitute the normal caster level check with a heal check (also with a bonus equal to your tier).<br /> <br /> <b>Body-Purifying Admonitions (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 3 ranks, Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> You can spend 5 motes to cast <i>neutralize poison</i> as a spell-like ability. When you cast <i>neutralize poison, </i>you always gain a bonus on your caster level check to remove the disease equal to your tier. You may substitute the normal caster level check with a heal check (also with a bonus equal to your Tier).<br /> <br /> <b>Wholeness-Restoring Meditation (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Heal 4 ranks, Tier 3, Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> For 8 hours you provide miraculous, supernatural medical care to the target by spending 7 motes. When this time is up, your treatment duplicates the effects of <i>greater restoration</i> or <i>regeneration,</i> your choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Instant Treatment Methodology (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Flawless Diagnosis Technique, Heal 2 ranks<br /> This ability supplements a heal check to perform long-term care or any other heal check that takes up to an hour. If spend 3 motes to activate this ability and provide long-term care, you do so in 10 minutes, after which the patient receives the full benefits of long-term care, but can still only gain these benefits once every 8 hours. You can use this ability to accelerate any heal check that normally takes up to an hour to perform by spending 3 motes. If you do, you can perform that check as a full-round action instead.<br /> <br /> <b>The Magic Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Adamant Circle Sorcery (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Spellcraft 2 ranks, Knowledge (Arcana) 2 ranks, Tier 2,<br /> Select three spells from the sorcerer/wizard spell list no higher than 9<sup>th</sup> level. You can cast those spells by spending motes equal to the spell level. Your caster level for these spells equals twice your Tier. You must have a minimum intelligence score of (10 + the spell level) and a minimum Tier equal to the spell level in order to cast spells in this way. The save DC of these spells is (10 + the spell level + your Intelligence modifier).You can select this ability multiple times. If you do, you gain three more spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Mythic Spellcasting (Ex)</b>: <i>Prerequisites: </i>Spellcraft 3 ranks<br /> This ability works like the Mythic Spellcasting universal path ability. You can learn a number of mythic spells equal to your tier and can expend Essence when casting them to enhance the results. To select a mythic spell, you must be able to cast the non-mythic version or have it on your list of spells known. Every time you gain a new tier, you can select an additional mythic spell. You can take this ability up to three times. Each additional time you take it, you can select an additional number of spells equal to your Tier and you gain one additional mythic spell whenever you gain a tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Detecting Glance (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (the Planes) 2 ranks.<br /> You can cast <i>see invisibility </i>as a spell-like ability for three motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Cutting Attack (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (the Planes) 2 ranks, Spirit-Detecting Glance<br /> You can spend one mote when you make an attack to give all your attacks that round the <i>ghost touch </i>quality. Such attacks also affect creatures on the ethereal plane as if they were in an analogous position in the material plane. Such attacks ignore the DR of outsiders, incorporeal undead and intelligent undead for two additional motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Ghost-Eating Technique (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (the Planes) 4 ranks, Tier 3<br /> You may supplement an attack for three motes so that it may even slay immortals. This ability affects creatures that normally resurrect after being slain or return to their home plane or some other sanctum when they die. It affects everything from vampires with defensive gaseous forms to Great Old Ones with Immortality. Creatures hit by an attack supplemented with this charm are subject to the effects of a <i>dimensional anchor.</i> Additionally, for the duration of this spell-like ability, powers that grant functional immortality as above (subject to GM discretion) to the target are suppressed.<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit-Repelling Diagram (Sp/Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (the Planes) 3 ranks, Spirit-Cutting Attack<br /> As spell-like abilities for 3 motes, you can cast <i>magic circle against chaos</i> if you are lawful, <i>magic circle against evil</i> if you are good, <i>magic circle against law</i> if you are chaotic and <i>magic circle against good</i> if you are evil. You can spend one mote to enhance a <i>magic circle </i>you have already cast as a free action. When enhanced in this way, creatures that the <i>magic circle </i>protects against can be affected as if corporeal by creatures within the circle, and cannot enter the ethereal plane. If an ethereal creature the <i>magic circle </i>protects against enters the area of effect it immediately enters the material plane. When you enhance a <i>magic circle </i>spell in this way, creatures with a higher Mythic Rank or Mythic Tier than yourself are allowed one will save (DC 13 plus your Intelligence modifier) to negate the effect, but if they fail they may not attempt to save again for 8 hours. If you are a spellcaster you can substitute the ability modifier tied to your spell\u2019s save DCs instead of your intelligence modifier to calculate the save DC of this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>All-Encompassing Sorcerer\u2019s Sight (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (the Planes) 3 ranks, Spellcraft 3 ranks, Spirit-Detecting Glance.<br /> You can cast <i>true seeing </i>for 5 motes and can cast <i>detect magic </i>at-will. These are both spell-like abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerer\u2019s Burning Chakra Charm (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Knowledge (the Planes) 4 ranks, Spellcraft 6 ranks, Tier 3, All-Encompassing Sorcerer\u2019s Sight.<br /> You can use All-Encompassing Sorcerer\u2019s Sight to cast <i>true seeing </i>for one mote. Whenever your Anima Banner is at the 8-mote level or higher, you can cast <i>true seeing </i>in this way at-will instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-06-2015, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:54:32-07:00","id":542050,"title":"","content":"<b>(Part 3)<br /> <br /> (Updated 6/7/15)<br /> <br /> The Night Caste</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Night Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Tier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Hidden Sun Anima Mastery, Night Dominion Ability,</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Night Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Night Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Night Dominion Ability</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Bonus Hit Points:</b> Whenever you gain a Night Caste tier, you gain 5 bonus hit points. These hit points stack with themselves and don't affect your overall Hit Dice or other statistics.<br /> <br /> <b>Dark Sun Anima Mastery (Su):</b> You have more control over your anima banner than most Exalts, and can use it to hide yourself. You always gain an enhancement bonus on stealth and slight of hand checks equal to your Tier. Additionally, when you spend Peripheral Essence on a mythic spell, mythic Feat, or other ability, you may choose to spend half again the amount normally required by that ability. If you do, spending that Essence does not affect your Anima Banner. This effect itself never affects your anima banner either.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Dominion Ability:</b> Every Tier, you learn one Solar Dominion Ability or Supernatural Martial Arts Technique. These Dominion Abilities can be from your own Caste or any other Solar Caste. Starting at the 1<sup>st</sup> Tier and every three Tiers thereafter (4<sup>th</sup>, 7<sup>th</sup>, and 10<sup>th</sup>) this Dominion Ability must be a Night Dominion Ability. Note that some Dominion Abilities are spell-like abilities and unless stated otherwise, these Dominion Abilities function at a Caster Level equal to twice your Tier. The Night Dominions are Prowess, Awareness, Evasion, Trickery, and Shadows.<br /> <br /> <b>Path Abilities as Dominion Abilities: </b>Note that some Dominion Abilities function like analogous Mythic Path Abilities. These abilities mechanically identical, but the Tier requirements use the Tier requirements of the Dominion Ability, not the associated Path Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>The Prowess Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Graceful Crane Stance (Ex and Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Acrobatics 2 ranks.<br /> You can spend 3 motes to gain perfect, supernatural balance for 20 minutes per Tier. You gain a +20 competence bonus on any acrobatics check to maintain your balance. Additionally, you can keep your footing on anything as strong and wide as a human hair. You treat all surfaces that are at least that strong and wide as three foot wide ledges capable of supporting one thousand pounds of weight.<br /> <br /> <b>Monkey Leap Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Acrobatics 2 ranks.<br /> By spending 3 motes you enhance your jumping ability for a number of minutes equal to twice your Tier. During this time, double the results of all your Acrobatics checks made to jump.<br /> <br /> <b>Soaring Crane Leap (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Acrobatics 3 ranks, Monkey Leap Technique<br /> You can spend 2 motes to enhance a single Acrobatics check made to jump. Multiply the result of that check by five. This does not stack with the multiplier of Monkey Leap Technique<br /> <br /> <b>Mountain-Crossing Leap Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Acrobatics 6 ranks, Soaring Crane Leap.<br /> You can spend five motes to safely jump up to (your Tier times 5) miles, beginning this jump as a full-round action. During this jump you move at a rate of one mile every minute.<br /> <br /> <b>Foe-Vaulting Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Acrobatics 2 ranks, Monkey Leap Technique<br /> You can spend one mote to gain a +10 competence bonus on an acrobatics check made to leave an opponent\u2019s threatened area.<br /> <br /> <b>Thunderbolt Attack Prana (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Acrobatics 6 ranks,<br /> You gain Fleet Warrior, as per the Champion Path Ability:<br /> <i>Fleet Warrior (Ex): </i>When making a full attack, you can move up to your speed either before or after your attacks. This movement provokes attacks of opportunity as normal.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Speed (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dex 15<br /> You can spend three motes to increase your base movement speed for 2 minutes per Tier. Your base movement speed increases by 10 feet during this time. This bonus speed increases to 15 feet at 4<sup>th</sup> Tier, 20 feet at 7<sup>th</sup> Tier and 25 feet at 10<sup>th</sup> Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Racing Hare Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dex 15, Con 15, Lightning Speed<br /> This ability can be used to supplement distance running to cover vast amounts of ground quickly for 6 motes. You can run at speeds of ([Your Tier + your Constitution modifier] x10) miles per hour for up to one hour. If your distance running is interrupted during this time, you are considered to be under the effects of Lightning Speed instead of this ability until either this ability\u2019s duration expires or you resume the trip.<br /> <br /> <b>Spider-Foot Style (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Climb 2 ranks,<br /> You gain the benefits of <i>spider climb, </i>save that this is an exceptional ability rather than a spell or spell-like ability and you needn\u2019t have your hands free to use this ability. Your effective caster level for this ability is equal to twice your Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Feather-Foot Style (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Graceful Crane Stance, Acrobatics 2 ranks<br /> Surfaces support your weight as if you weighed no more than a feather. This allows you to move across such improbable surfaces as wet paper, liquids, lava or swarms of Fine creatures. These surfaces are effectively solid, but not necessarily harmless for you to move across.<br /> <br /> <b>Eagle Wing Style (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Spider-Foot Style, Feather-Foot Style, Acrobatics 6 ranks, Climb 2 ranks, Fly 1 rank, Tier 3<br /> For two motes, your flight speed improves by 30 feet and your maneuverability increases by one step. If you do not have a fly speed, you may spend three motes to gain a fly speed of 30 feet with poor maneuverability.<br /> <br /> <b>Increasing Strength Exercise (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1<br /> You can cast <i>bull\u2019s strength </i>as a spell-like ability for one mote, but only on yourself.<br /> <br /> <b>The Awareness Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Keen Sight Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Perception 2 ranks.<br /> For three motes, you gain a bonus on perception checks equal to your tier, so long as you are not blinded and sight is relevant to the check. You also gain low-light vision, and Darkvision for 120 feet. These effects last 2 minutes per tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Keen Hearing and Touch Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Perception 2 ranks<br /> For three motes, you gain a bonus on perception checks equal to your tier, so long as you are not deafened and hearing is relevant to the check. You also gain Tremorsense for 30 feet. These effects last 2 minutes per tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Keen Smell Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Perception 2 ranks.<br /> For three motes, you gain a bonus on perception checks equal to your tier, so long as you can smell and what you are trying to find or notice isn\u2019t odorless. You also gain the Scent special quality. These effects last 2 minutes per tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Unsurpassed Senses Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Perception 2 ranks. Keen Smell Technique, Keen Hearing and Touch Technique, or Keen Sight Technique.<br /> You always gain a bonus on perception checks equal to your tier, which stacks with the bonus provided by this ability\u2019s prerequisite abilities.<br /> <br /> <b>Surprise Anticipation Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Perception 5 ranks.<br /> You may spend one mote whenever you are caught flat footed or are unable to act in a surprise round. If you do, you are no longer flat-footed and can act as if you weren\u2019t surprised. This ability does not cause you to automatically perceive creatures using stealth, but you are instinctually aware of some kind of danger when you otherwise would be surprised.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye of the Unconquered Sun (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 6, Perception 11 ranks, Keen Sight Technique, Unsurpassed Senses Technique.<br /> You can cast <i>true seeing </i>as a spell-like ability for 9 motes. In addition, for the duration of the ability, you gain a +20 insight bonus on all perception and sense motive checks. Your Anima Banner also flares to the 19+ mote level, and does not decrease in intensity until this ability ends.<br /> <br /> <b>The Evasion Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Over Water (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dex 13, Tier 1<br /> You may spend one mote as an immediate action in response to an attack you are aware of. If you are taking any penalties to your AC, you do not take penalties to your AC against that attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Seven Shadows Evasion (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dex 13, Dodge, Tier 1, Shadow Over Water<br /> You may spend three motes as an immediate action in response to an attack before the attack roll is made. If you do, you gain a +20 dodge bonus to your AC against that attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Reflexive Sidestep Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dex 13, Tier 1<br /> You may spend one mote as an immediate action in response to an attack you are flat-footed against. If you do, you gain Uncanny Dodge (as per the rouge class feature) against that attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Flow Like Blood (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dex 13, Dodge, Reflexive Sidestep Technique, Tier 1<br /> You may spend 4 motes as a standard action. If you do, you gain Uncanny Dodge and Improved Uncanny Dodge (as per the rogue class features) for 2 minutes per Tier. Your effective rogue level for this ability equals twice your Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Leaping Dodge Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Dodge, Mobility, Dex 13, Tier 1 or; Lightning Reflexes, Dex 13, Tier 1 or; the Evasion Class Feature<br /> Once per turn, when you are missed by an attack or successfully make a Reflex saving throw, you may leap 10 feet per Tier in a direction you choose as an immediate action. If this movement takes you out of the area of the effect you made a reflex save against, you completely negate the effect. If you have the Evasion class feature, you may use this Charm even on a failed reflex save. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity.<br /> <b>The Trickery Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Flawlessly Impenetrable Disguise (Sp): </b>Disguise 2 ranks, Tier 1<br /> You can cast <i>disguise self </i>as a spell-like ability for 1 mote. Creatures that interact with your disguise take a -4 penalty on will saves to disbelieve the illusion. The save DC for this ability is 10 plus your Tier plus your intelligence or charisma modifier (whichever is higher).<br /> <br /> <b>Perfect Mirror (Su): </b>Prerequisites: Tier 3, ability to cast <i>disguise self</i> as a spell or spell like ability.<br /> Whenever you cast <i>disguise self</i> the spell\u2019s bonus on disguise checks increases from a +10 to a +20. If you are imitating a specific creature you are familiar with, you imitate their mannerisms perfectly, granting you a +20 bonus on bluff checks to avoid being compromised as long as the spell or ability is active. Finally, as long as the creature has a humanoid body shape and is the same size category as you, you can use <i>disguise self</i> to imitate a creature with a different creature type.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Pickpocketing Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Slight of Hand 2 ranks.<br /> You can spend 3 motes to gain a +20 competence bonus when making a slight of hand check to steal an item.<br /> <br /> <b>Lock-Opening Touch (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Disable Device 2 ranks<br /> You can spend 3 motes to gain a +20 competence bonus on a disable device check to open a lock. You are considered to have thieves\u2019 tools for the purposes of this roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Trap-Disarming Gesture (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Disable Device 2 ranks, Lock-Opening Touch<br /> You can spend 3 motes to gain a +20 competence bonus on a disable device check to disarm a trap. You are considered to have thieves\u2019 tools for the purposes of this roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Door-Evading Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Lock-Opening Gesture, Disable Device 6 ranks.<br /> When making a move action, you can spend 10 motes to move through a closed and/or locked portal, as long as you have enough movement to move completely past it. This Charm only allows you to pass through portals; things designed for creatures to travel through, such as doors, gates, or portcullises; you cannot use it to gain access to the contents of a locked chest or to pass through a fortress wall, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>The Shadows Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Easily Overlooked Presence Method (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Stealth 2 ranks<br /> By spending 3 motes, for the next 2 times your tier minutes, creatures must make a will save (DC 20 plus your Tier) to notice you unless battle readiness or some other circumstance makes you obvious. In addition, this Charm will automatically fail if an observer has a circumstance or insight bonus to notice you of +2 or higher. This is an illusion effect.<br /> <br /> <b>Vanishing From the Mind\u2019s Eye Method (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Stealth 6 ranks, Easily Overlooked Presence Method<br /> For 10 motes, you can erase yourself from the memories of anyone who has seen you in the last 24 times your Tier hours as a full-round action. You can choose to omit specific creatures from this effect, but everyone else must make a Will save (DC equals your Stealth bonus plus 7) or they simply forget you were there. Creatures that engaged you in combat or some other, strenuous contest gain a +4 bonus to this save, and if they fail, they remember the contest or combat, but the specifics about their opponent are completely different; their minds imagine a new, detailed adversary.<br /> <br /> <b>Invisible Statue Spirit (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Stealth 2 ranks<br /> By spending 6 motes as a standard action, you are effected by <i>sequester, </i>as the spell, until you take another action, though you are remain concise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Eclipse Caste</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Eclipse Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Tier</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Caste Features</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1<sup>st</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Sanctified Oath, , Eclipse Dominion Ability,</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2<sup>nd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3<sup>rd</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Eclipse Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Eclipse Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Solar Dominion Ability</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10<sup>th</sup></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Eclipse Dominion Ability</td> </tr> </table></div> <b>Bonus Hit Points: </b>Whenever you gain an Eclipse Caste tier, you gain 4 bonus hit points. These hit points stack with themselves and don't affect your overall Hit Dice or other statistics.<br /> <br /> <b>Sanctified Oath (Sp):</b> By spending 10 motes when you are party to, or an official witness of an agreement, you sanctify the oath in heaven\u2019s eyes. When this happens, ancient runes and treaties of heaven coalesce from your anima and swirl around you, written in Celestial (or Old Realm, if more appropriate to the campaign setting). If an Oath you have sanctified in this way is broken (even by you), heaven will punish the oath-breaker. Firstly, remaining parties are released from the oath if it is no longer viable, and haven notifies them (via <i>sending</i>) that they are no longer bound to the oath. Secondly, heaven ensures the oath-breaker gains as little benefit as possible from breaking the oath. An ally may sell out your army for an Empress\u2019 ransom, only for the gold to be lost in a storm while in-transit, or simply destroyed by a pillar of divine fire. Lastly, the oath-breaker is punished in a spectacular method by heaven. Usually, at a time critically inconvenient to the oath-breaker, the oath-breaker is subject to the effects of an appropriate, harmful, 7<sup>th</sup> to 9<sup>th</sup> level spell (this could be anything from a <i>dictum</i> on a particularly deceptive oath-breaker, to a <i>meteor swarm</i> on an oath-breaking warlord at the moment before his triumph). The effective caster level for this spell is always 20, attack rolls this spell calls for are made at an attack bonus of +40, and the oath-breaker always takes a -20 on any saving throws made to resist its effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Solar Dominion Ability:</b> Every Tier, you learn one Solar Dominion Ability or Supernatural Martial Arts Technique. These Dominion Abilities can be from your own Caste or any other Solar Caste. Starting at the 1<sup>st</sup> Tier and every three Tiers thereafter (4<sup>th</sup>, 7<sup>th</sup>, and 10<sup>th</sup>) this Dominion Ability must be a Eclipse Dominion Ability. Note that some Dominion Abilities are spell-like abilities, unless stated otherwise these Dominion Abilities function at a Caster Level equal to twice your Tier. The Eclipse Dominions are Governance, Linguistics, Ride, Sail and Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Path Abilities as Dominion Abilities: </b>Note that some Dominion Abilities function like analogous Mythic Path Abilities. These abilities mechanically identical, but the Tier requirements use the Tier requirements of the Dominion Ability, not the associated Path Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Governance Dominion Abilities</b><br /> <br /> <b>Frugal Merchant Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequsites: </i>Tier 1, Appraise 2 ranks<br /> You can spend a single mote when making an appraise check to understand a product\u2019s quality and condition (whether it\u2019s broken, cursed, destroyed, damaged, masterwork, diseased, poisoned, expired, ect). This ability can discern that an item is magical or cursed. If you can test a weapon or on try on armor, you can also tell its enhancement bonus/penalty, but you cannot discern specific magical weapon or armor qualities. Use of this ability also grants you a +3 insight bonus when you haggle to buy or sell the object, and a +9 insight bonus on sense motive checks against someone trying to deceive you about the object. These bonuses persist until the market value of the item changes significantly for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> <b>Insightful Buyer Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Appraise 2 ranks<br /> You can spend three motes whenever you try to buy, sell, or trade something wisely. If you do, you understand the object\u2019s market price in any relevant market you have at least passing familiarity with. With this understanding, you also gain an understanding on how to reduce penalties to rolls to buy or sell a product from trade barriers, volatile markets, and other obstacles by an amount equal to your Tier, though this reduction usually requires action on your part, at GM discretion. Additionally, when using this ability, your skill with haggling is such that you treat customers and vendors as friendly for the purposes of item price.<br /> <br /> <b>Speed the Wheels (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Diplomacy 2 ranks, Tier 1<br /> When you earn Influence or Labor capital in downtime, you can spend 4 motes per day to multiply the capital gained by your Tier (minimum 2). Additional capital gained in this way (Influence beyond what you would normally earn without this ability) is tracked in a separate Speed the Wheels pool, and can only be spent to pay for downtime activities, such as recruiting teams or constructing rooms. Additionally, you may spend 8 motes to manage a bureaucratic process (paperwork, legislation, etc.). If you do, progress on that process over time is multiplied by your Tier (minimum 2).<br /> <br /> <b>Bureau-Rectifying Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3; Diplomacy or Profession 6 ranks<br /> You may spend 8 motes to spend 1d6 days removing corruption and incompetence from a bureaucratic organization you have authority to lead, manage, or direct. Your reforms remove the least effective and most corrupt members of an organization immediately. Additionally, any loss in profit or productivity the organization was suffering from is permanently reduced by 20%, which stacks; 5 uses of this ability could reduce organizational corruption by 100% if no new corrupting influences are introduced to the organization.<br /> When using the kingdom building rules, this ability indefinitely reduces the cost of edicts, buildings and terrain improvements by 5% per use (maximum 15%, representing an organization completely purged of corruption) and indefinitely reduce consumption by one per hex per 2 uses (maximum 2 per hex). If you are with an army and have authority over its supplies and pay, this ability indefinitely reduces its consumption by 1 per size category, which does not stack. Your GM can choose to track fractional BP generated by this ability as GP, or to simply round to the nearest whole BP.<br /> One use of this ability negates and is negated by one use of Four the Air Argument Technique.<br /> <br /> <b>Indolent Official Charm (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1; Diplomacy, Bluff, Profession or Intimidate, 2 ranks<br /> This ability exploits the sloth and corruption in your enemies. You can spend half an hour communicating with an organization about a project; the GM is the authority on how much of the organization must be present for this ability to succeed, though underlings count as present if their direct supervisor is present. If the ability is successful, multiply the amount of time remaining on finishing the project by your Tier. At GM discretion, a heroic character with significant authority over and a vested interest in the project may make an appropriate skill check (such as diplomacy, intimidate, or a relevant profession) to have the project proceed at normal speed (DC of this check equals 10 plus your Tier plus your HD plus your Intelligence or Charisma modifier).<br /> <br /> <b>Four the Air Argument Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Diplomacy or Profession 6 ranks, Indolent Official Charm<br /> You spend 8 motes and 1d6 days spreading corruption and incompetence in a bureaucratic organization you could reasonably influence. The organization immediately begins losing 10% of its productivity or profit indefinitely, which stacks up to five times; an organization suffering from 5 uses of this ability could be losing 50% of its profits to corruption and inefficiency.<br /> Lengthy investigation and/or magic (judicious use of <i>zone of truth, charm person </i>or <i>geas/quest</i> makes a very effective countermeasure to this ability) can remove this corruption, but any skill checks made to do so should have a DC equal to 10 plus your Tier plus your Intelligence or Charisma modifier.<br /> When using the kingdom building rules, this ability indefinitely increases the cost of edicts, buildings, and terrain improvements by 5% per use (maximum 15%, representing a bureaucracy where practically every official is destructively self-interested) and indefinitely increases consumption by one per hex per two uses (maximum 2 per hex). If used on an army, this ability indefinitely increases its consumption by one per size category, which does not stack. Your GM can choose to track fractional BP generated by this ability as GP, or to simply round to the nearest whole BP.<br /> One use of this ability negates and is negated by one use a Bureau-Rectifying Method.<br /> <br /> <b>The Linguistics Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Whirling Brush Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1; Linguistics 1 rank or Profession (scribe) 1 rank<br /> You can spend 3 motes to write 10 times your tier faster. This ability does not merely allow you to move your stylus across a page faster, it also increases the pace at which you compose manuscript, for example; in addition to simply transcribing a manuscript 30 times faster, a Tier 3 Solar with this ability could draft and edit Declaration of Independence in a day when such deliberations might normally take her a month. This ability affects the time it takes you to scribe scrolls and/or write down new content into a spell book or formula book. Whenever you add additional spells or formulae into a book when you level up, you gain your Tier in additional spells for free.<br /> <br /> <b>Flawless Brush Discipline (Ex and Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3; Linguistics 6 ranks or Profession (scribe) 6 ranks<br /> You can spend 3 motes to gain a +20 on any profession (scribe) check regarding calligraphy, or any other skill check regarding calligraphy at the GM\u2019s discretion. You can spend 4 motes to make any calligraphy you\u2019ve prepared in this way particularly enchanting. Creatures who read calligraphy so enchanted are subject to <i>charm monster </i>(Will negates, DC 10 plus your Tier plus your Charisma modifier) if they read the work for at least 4 minutes within the next 24 hours.<br /> <br /> <b>Letter-Within-a-Letter Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1; Linguistics 2 ranks or Bluff 2 ranks<br /> You can include a secret, coded message within another written work you compose. Only the intended recipients can read the message. This is an Illusion and Enchantment effect. If a creature that can see through Illusions and is immune to enchantments can read this message normally.<br /> <br /> <b>Discerning Savant\u2019s Eye (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Linguistics 2 ranks or Sense Motive 2 ranks<br /> For 5 motes, you understand coded, obscured, unclear or hidden communication as if it was clear. This includes things such as faded text inscribed in stone, a man with a mangled tongue attempting speech, or a coded exchange between spies at a gala. You can make out such communication as if it were in its original language, although you still must know that language to understand it.<br /> <br /> <b>Sagacious Reading of Intent (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Linguistics or Sense Motive 2 ranks<br /> You can spend 1 mote to gain a +5 insight bonus to any single Sense Motive check. You can spend 4 motes to make a Sense Motive check opposed by your target\u2019s Bluff (which you can then spend a further 1 mote on to gain a +5, as above) whenever your target makes a statement. If you succeed, the GM or player of that character must give you a one-sentence summary of what your target hopes to achieve with this statement.<br /> <br /> <b>Excellent Emissary\u2019s Tongue (Ex or Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Linguistics 6 ranks<br /> You can communicate effectively with creatures whose language you are familiar with, even if you do not actually know that language, as an exceptional ability. Make a linguistics check for every page you read or every 6 minutes of conversation. The DC of this check is 15 if you have been spending the last couple of days studying or hearing the language, DC 20 if you have only spent the last few hours studying or hearing the language, or DC 25 if you\u2019ve spent no significant amount of time with the language, and at that point, this is a supernatural ability, not an exceptional ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Twisted Words Technique (Ex and Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 6, Letter-Within a Letter Technique, Sagacious Reading of Intent, Flawless Brush Discipline; Linguistics, Profession (Scribe), Bluff, or Diplomacy, 12 ranks<br /> This ability works as per Flawless Brush Discipline, but the target is affected by <i>lesser geas </i>(Will negates, DC 10 plus your Tier plus your Charisma modifier) instead of <i>charm monster. </i>This spell-like ability can affect a creature of any Hit Dice that fails its save. The orders for this <i>lesser geas</i> must be within the written work.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbreakable Fascination Method (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3; Perform (Oratory) 6 ranks, Excellent Emissary\u2019s Tongue<br /> You can use Unbreakable Fascination Method any time you begin some kind of performance or oration for 10 motes. If you do, your anima flares to the 19+ mote level until you choose to end this charm. Creatures that can perceive your performance or oration clearly must make a will save (DC 10 plus your Tier plus your Charisma modifier) each turn they wish to act normally. Creatures without magical defenses with less HD than your Tier fail this save automatically. A creature that fails this save gains the fascinated condition for that round. Creatures that save against a given use of this ability a number of times equal to twice your Tier are immune to its effects for the duration. This ability ends when you stop performing or orating, though you may make a dramatic pause.<br /> <br /> <b>The Ride Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Master Horseman\u2019s Techniques: </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Ride 2 ranks<br /> When you select this dominion ability, choose up to two of the following benefits. You may select this Dominion Ability multiple times. Its effects do not stack; each time you do, you gain a different benefit. For the purposes of these abilities, a mount is either a creature trained to serve as a mount, or a creature currently being directed via the Ride skill.<br /> <i>Harmony of Spirits Style (Ex): </i>You can spend one mote as an immediate actions whenever you would normally fall or be knocked from a mount. If you do, you stay mounted. As a permanent benefit, you never have a chance to fall from a mount for being unconscious.<br /> <i>Horse-Summoning Whistle (Su): </i>You can spend one mote to magically call a mount or animal companion to you to your side. The mount in question makes its way toward you as best it can. If this travel puts the mount in question in immediate danger, it is allowed a will save (DC 10 plus your Tier plus your Charisma modifier) to resist the effect. This ability only effects creatures with an intelligence of 2 or less, unless that mount is a bonded mount or animal companion.<br /> <i>Master Horseman\u2019s Eye (Su): </i>You can spend one mote when evaluating a mount. If you do, you know the ability scores, feats, Hit Dice, Remaining HP, creature type, CR, subtypes, saves and skills of that creature.<br /> <i>Speed Sustaining Technique (Su): </i>You can spend one mote as a free action to enhance the stamina of a mount for two hours. For the duration, the mount gains your Tier as a morale bonus on fortitude saves, will not become fatigued or exhausted (but remains so if already fatigued or exhausted), and does not suffer harmful, random incidents from travel such as thrown shoes or injured hooves.<br /> <i>Spirit-Steadying Assurances (Su): </i>You can spend 1 mote as an immediate action whenever your mount makes a Wills save against fear. If you do, your mount gains a +20 to that save.<br /> <br /> <b>Single Spirit Method (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Ride 6 ranks, Worthy Mount Technique<br /> You can affect your mount with your spells that have a range of \u201cpersonal\u201d. When used in this way, those spells have a range of \u201ctouch\u201d instead. Additionally, you can have your mount use any of your Dominion Abilities that are immediate actions or are some kind of reaction (at GM discretion) using your Essence pools. You can have your mount use any other Dominion Ability of yours it meets the prerequisites for and could perform with its anatomy, using your mote pools, on its turn, ignoring Tier prerequisites and prerequisite Dominion Abilities. Dominion abilities used in this way have a 1 mote surcharge.<br /> <br /> <b>Phantom Steed (Sp): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Ride 6 ranks, Master Horseman\u2019s Techniques<br /> You can cast <i>phantom steed </i>as a spell-like ability for 3 motes.<br /> <br /> <b>Wind-Racing Essence Infusion (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Ride 6 ranks<br /> You spend 5 motes to imbue your mount with infinite energy for two hours. Your horse is no longer fatigued or exhausted, and is immune to fatigue and exhaustion. Secondly, this ability adds your Tier to your mount\u2019s acrobatics checks to jump and maintain balance. Your mount\u2019s speed increases by 40 feet at 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier, and 80 feet at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Sometimes Horses Fly Approach (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Ride 6 ranks, Wind-Racing Essence Infusion<br /> By spending 5 motes as a free action, you can give your mount the ability to fly, as well as the confidence to do so. Your mount gains a fly speed equal to its movement speed for one hour.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sail Dominion</b><br /> <br /> <b>Salty Dog Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Profession (Sailor) 2 ranks<br /> By spending 4 motes, you gain enhanced maritime acumen for two hours per Tier. While on a ship, you add +2 to your attack and damage rolls, and add your Tier to acrobatics checks, diplomacy checks, sense motive checks, profession (sailor) checks, perception checks, and climb checks. Additionally, you add +2 to your saving throws while on a ship at 1<sup>st</sup> Tier, +3 at 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier, and +4 at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier. None of these benefits apply when the ship in question is in dry-dock, wrecked, on display in a museum, or otherwise completely inactive.<br /> <br /> <b>Invincible Admiral Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Profession (Sailor) 6 ranks, Salty Dog Method<br /> By spending 12 motes, you apply the benefits of your Salty Dog Method to creatures following your maritime orders for two hours per Tier. You can affect up to 100 creatures (or a medium army) at 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier, 500 creatures (or a huge army) at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier and 2000 creatures (or a colossal army) at 10<sup>th</sup> Tier. In mass combat, as long as every unit in the army could benefit from Salty Dog Method, the army gains a +2 bonus to OM, DV and morale checks at 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier. This bonus increases to +3 at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier and +4 at 10<sup>th</sup> Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Ship-Claiming Stance (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Profession (Sailor) 2 ranks<br /> You can spend 5 motes as a full-round action to claim a ship not currently owned by another magic-user (any creature with supernatural abilities, spell-like abilities, or spells). All other creatures on the ship gain 1 negative level (Will negates, DC 20) until you formally welcome them aboard and unless you later renounce them. Creatures lose this negative level immediately if they leave the ship. This ability is enforced by the little god of the ship, meaning you must welcome and renounce others in Old Realm (or Celestial, if more appropriate to the campaign setting) within earshot of your ship. The DC to save against negative level increases to 22 at 3<sup>rd</sup> Tier, 24 at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier, and 26 at 10<sup>th</sup> Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Hull-Preserving Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Profession (Sailor) 6 ranks, Ship-Claiming Stance<br /> You can activate this ability as an immediate action for 8 motes in response to a damage roll against a ship you are on or within. If you do, the ship takes no damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Perfect Reckoning Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Profession (Sailor) 2 ranks<br /> You can spend 3 motes to gain a +20 competence bonus on any Profession (Sailor) check or Perception check to navigate to a destination, notice hazards, or avoid hazards. This ability only functions while you are on a ship.<br /> <br /> <b>Storm-Weathering Essence Infusion (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Profession (Sailor) 2 ranks<br /> If you are authorized to coordinate or give orders to the crew of a ship, you may spend 6 motes to increase their ability to sustain the ship through dangerous hazards. Affected crew (yourself included) gain a +3 bonus on any d20 roll that directly serves to preserve the ship, its cargo, its pasengers and its crew. This could be anything from perception checks to notice hazardous reefs or attack rolls to fend off sahuagin raiders. This bonus increases to +4 at 6<sup>th</sup> Tier, and +5 at 10<sup>th</sup> Tier. These benefits last for 2 hours per Tier.<br /> <br /> <b>Sea Ambush Technique (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Profession (Sailor) 2 ranks, Stealth 2 ranks<br /> When you attempt to establish an ambush in maritime mass combat, you can spend 8 motes to add your Tier to your OM check, and your army can establish an ambush even if they do not have concealment.<br /> <br /> <b>The Charm Dominion:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Wise-Eyed Courtier Method (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Charisma 13<br /> By spending at least 24 cumulative hours (no more than 8 hours per day; treat this as a downtime activity) over the last year influencing a social group, you can change that group\u2019s alignment by one step, or convert it to the worship of a deity that is within one step of its alignment. This group cannot normally consist of more than 500 times your Tier people, but if you are the Ruler, Councilor, General, High Priest, Magister, or Spymaster of a kingdom, you can affect the entire kingdom regardless of its size. Additionally, if you are the commander of an army, you can affect that army with this ability regardless of its size.<br /> At the end of the year in which your manipulation has taken place, roll a Diplomacy, Bluff Perform (Oratory), or Intimidate check, as appropriate. If you succeed, the group\u2019s alignment changes by one step, or it adopts the worship of a new deity within one step of its alignment.<br /> This check is DC 15, although anyone in the group with HD equal to or greater than twice your Tier, or anyone in the group with a Mythic Rank or Mythic Tier can contest this roll with a Diplomacy, Perform (Oratory), Bluff or Intimidate check of their own. All creatures who qualify may make the check, if the check result of the highest creature\u2019s roll is greater than 15, that is the new DC use this ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Wild Revelry Approach (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Charisma 13<br /> You may spend 3 motes to rouse emotions in others as part of an oration or public debate. This oration or debate lasts 10 minutes per three motes spent. Creatures who see or hear you may make a Will save (DC 10 + your Tier + your Charisma modifier) if they fail, they begin to feel an emotion you desire for the duration of the ability + one hour per two Tiers you possess (minimum 1 additional hour). While the specific emotion felt can be as detailed as you wish (Such as the sadness emotion specifically expressed as hopelessness), they all have one of the following mechanical effects:<br /> <i>Anger: </i>Affected creatures benefit from <i>rage</i>, as the spell.<br /> <i>Sadness: </i>Each affected creature takes a -2 penalty to initiative rolls, perception checks and Will saves.<br /> <i>Happiness/Confidence: </i>Affected creatures receive a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls, Will saves, and all skill checks other than perception and sense motive. On perception and sense motive checks, affected creatures take a -2 penalty instead.<br /> <i>Fear: </i>Creatures take a -2 penalty to saves against fear and increase their level of fear by one step.<br /> <i>Compassion: </i>Affected creatures gain a +2 morale bonus on heal, diplomacy, knowledge (religion) and Aid Another checks but take a -2 penalty to sense motive checks. Affected creatures also treat their caster levels for conjuration (healing) spells and spell-like abilities as one level higher.<br /> <i>Hate: </i>If you are Charisma 17 and inspiring anger at a specific group of creatures (as defined the favored enemy ranger class feature), you may inspire hate instead. Against that group, affected creatures gain a +2 racial bonus on attack rolls, weapon damage rolls, Intimidate checks and Sense Motive checks against the targeted group.<br /> <br /> <b>Taboo Inflicting Diatribe (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Charisma 15, Wise-Eyed Courtier Method<br /> This Ability permanently upgrades Wise-Eyed Courtier Method. It reduces the amount of time necessary to use that ability from 24 cumulative hours in a given year to 8 hours in a given month, and its affects are applied at the end of the month, not the end of the year. Additionally, upon successful use of that ability, you may convert the social group in question to a philosophy within one step of its alignment instead of changing its alignment or deity. This may replace an existing philosophy, or, if reasonably compatible, exist alongside it.<br /> <br /> <b>Venomous Whispers Technique (Su): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Charisma 15, Taboo Inflicting Diatribe<br /> When you interact socially with a group for at least 6 minutes, during that time you may spend 10 motes and condemn one creature known to you and that group. That creature must make a Will save (DC 10 plus your Tier plus your Charisma modifier). If it fails, it subtracts twice your Tier from all Charisma checks and Charisma-based skill checks regarding the group for a number of hours equal to twice your Tier. You may affect a group no larger than your Tier times 50 creatures.<br /> <br /> <b>Understanding the Court (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 3, Sense Motive 6 ranks,<br /> When in a specific social environment (this can be anything from an Empress\u2019 court to a seedy tavern) you can spend 7 motes to make a DC 10 sense motive check after interacting with that group socially for at least 2 minutes. If successful, you build a perfect social profile of the people in that environment and their relationships to one another. As a result of this understanding and as long as conditions in that social environment have not changed significantly since you used this ability, you gain a +5 bonus to all sense motive checks pertinent to that social environment.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastery of Small Matters (Ex): </b><i>Prerequisites: </i>Tier 1, Diplomacy 2 ranks<br /> You can spend one mote when making any kind of social or haggling roll. If you do, you treat any creatures relevant to that roll as if their attitude was one step friendlier towards you.<br /> <br /> <b>New Mythic Feats</b><br /> <br /> <b>Snake Style (Mythic, Combat): </b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Snake Style, Improved Unarmed Strike, Acrobatics 1 rank, Sense Motive 3 ranks.<br /> <b>Benefit: </b>When using snake style, you can spend one use of Mythic Power to increase the Sense Motive bonus granted by Snake Style by 3. You retain this benefit only as long as you continue using Snake Style.<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Sidewind (Mythic, Combat):</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Improved Unarmed Strike, Snake Style, Snake Style (Mythic), Snake Sidewind, Acrobatics 3 ranks, Sense Motive 6 ranks.<br /> <b>Benefit: </b>When you spend a use of Mythic Power to use Mythic Snake Style, your CMD bonus VS trip, bonus on acrobatics saves to avoid being knocked prone, and bonus on Reflex saves to avoid being knocked prone from Snake Sidewind increase by your Tier. Additionally, when Snake Sidewind would allow you to make a 5 foot step as an immediate action, you can instead move up to half your speed as an immediate action.<br /> <br /> <b>Snake Fang (Mythic, Combat):</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Combat Reflexes, Improved Unarmed Strike, Snake Sidewind, Snake Style, Snake Style (Mythic), Snake Sidewind (Mythic), Snake Fang, Acrobatics 6 ranks, Sense Motive 9 ranks.<br /> <b>Benefit: </b>You can spend one use of Mythic Power as a free action when using Snake Style. If you do, successful attacks against you are treated as missed attacks for the purposes of Snake Fang until the start of your next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Crane Style (Mythic, Combat)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Crane Style, Improved Unarmed Strike; base attack bonus +2 or monk level 1<sup>st</sup><br /> <b>Benefit: </b>When using Crane Style, you can spend one use of mythic power as a free action. If you do, you take no penalties to your attack rolls from fighting defensively. You retain this benefit only as long as you continue to use Crane Style.<br /> <br /> <b>Crane Wing (Mythic, Combat)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Crane Style, Crane Style (Mythic), Dodge, Improved Unarmed Strike, base attack bonus +5 or monk level 5<sup>th.</sup><br /> <b>Benefit: </b>Once per round, you can spend one use of mythic power to increase the dodge bonus granted by Crane Wing against one attack to +20.<br /> <br /> <b>Crane Riposte (Mythic, Combat)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Crane Style, Crane Wing, Crane Wing (Mythic), Dodge, Improved Unarmed Strike, base attack bonus +8 or monk level 7th.<br /> <b>Benefit: </b>When using Mythic Crane Style, your Crane Riposte resolves against your opponent\u2019s flat-footed AC, and the second attack that misses you in a round also provokes an attack of opportunity from you (which also resolves against flat-footed AC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-09-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-05T19:59:05-07:00","id":542052,"title":"","content":"Well, it's playable. There's a starter Mythic adventure in <i>Mythic Adventures,</i> and if anyone wants to run a half-Solar, half-Mythic Heroes party to see how they stack up against each other and give me a playtest report on the results, that'd be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:54:31-07:00","id":542810,"title":"","content":"Well holy crap, you actually made it through every Charm. I was curious to see if you'd make it all the way through. It seems like a great idea and I'd love to help play test. Any desire to do an online game?<br /> <br /> If I had a critique at first glance, it's that I believe the number of Charms to be excessive. For total conversions, more abstract homebrew to capture the feel and not all the meat seems like a better plan. Not only do your fighters have a gagillion feats, now they have Dominions as well. DnD/Pathfinder are very crunchy games, and bolting on all this makes stuff very complicated.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but Pathfinder isn't a perfect system. The &quot;tiers&quot; concept is well documented and I'm pretty much a believer in it.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I believe this is a fool's errand! I have misgivings, but you clearly put a ton of work into this. I'm really curious to see if a Fighter can actually stand up to a Wizard through the use of Dominions.<br /> <br /> Have you gotten any real playtime? How do you feel about the tiers concept?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T12:23:06-07:00","id":542851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Childofthesun1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/542004-pathfinder-mythic-solars-playtest-actually-playable?p=542810#post542810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well holy crap, you actually made it through every Charm. I was curious to see if you'd make it all the way through. It seems like a great idea and I'd love to help play test. Any desire to do an online game?<br /> <br /> If I had a critique at first glance, it's that I believe the number of Charms to be excessive. For total conversions, more abstract homebrew to capture the feel and not all the meat seems like a better plan. Not only do your fighters have a gagillion feats, now they have Dominions as well. DnD/Pathfinder are very crunchy games, and bolting on all this makes stuff very complicated.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but Pathfinder isn't a perfect system. The &quot;tiers&quot; concept is well documented and I'm pretty much a believer in it.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I believe this is a fool's errand! I have misgivings, but you clearly put a ton of work into this. I'm really curious to see if a Fighter can actually stand up to a Wizard through the use of Dominions.<br /> <br /> Have you gotten any real playtime? How do you feel about the tiers concept?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None of this has been playtested yet. I only finished this draft last night. When I have time, I'd like to run <i>Fire Over Blackcrag</i> with a mixed party of mythic heroes and Exalts to see how they stack up against one another, but that'll be after my <i>Wrath of the Righteous </i>campaign ends.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, I'm working on the mythic versions of a few more combat style feats as a precursor to a proper, purpose-written playtest module set in Creation.<br /> <br /> Is your critique that there are too many Dominion Abilities, or that Solars get too many of them per tier? Solars only get 5-10, depending how many times you choose to take a Dominion Ability instead of a mythic feat.<br /> <br /> I'm in too many games to take part in a Playtest myself at the moment. But if anyone wants to run a mythic module or Adventure Path like <i>Fire Over Blackcrag</i> using Solars and tell me how it goes, I'd appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Also, this was <b>very time consuming</b>, but not as much work as you might think; a lot of this has been lifted/inspired from Pathfinder's <i>Mythic Adventures.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-06-2015, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:05:55-07:00","id":543087,"title":"","content":"I'm going to share this writeup with my exalted/Pathfinder players and see if they'd be willing to test it doing a game with Exalt-path characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe I can have some good feedback for you in a few weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T21:44:17-07:00","id":543463,"title":"","content":"This looks really cool, but I don't think I'll really be able to try this out with my group anytime soon. I'll shoot it over to them though and see what they think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T23:16:45-07:00","id":543490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ranger_Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/542004-pathfinder-mythic-solars-playtest-actually-playable?p=542851#post542851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> None of this has been playtested yet. I only finished this draft last night. When I have time, I'd like to run <i>Fire Over Blackcrag</i> with a mixed party of mythic heroes and Exalts to see how they stack up against one another, but that'll be after my <i>Wrath of the Righteous </i>campaign ends.<br /> <br /> In the mean time, I'm working on the mythic versions of a few more combat style feats as a precursor to a proper, purpose-written playtest module set in Creation.<br /> <br /> Is your critique that there are too many Dominion Abilities, or that Solars get too many of them per tier? Solars only get 5-10, depending how many times you choose to take a Dominion Ability instead of a mythic feat.<br /> <br /> I'm in too many games to take part in a Playtest myself at the moment. But if anyone wants to run a mythic module or Adventure Path like <i>Fire Over Blackcrag</i> using Solars and tell me how it goes, I'd appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Also, this was <b>very time consuming</b>, but not as much work as you might think; a lot of this has been lifted/inspired from Pathfinder's <i>Mythic Adventures.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about the sheer volume of them, and upon further examination, their questionable balance. I mean, sure, in Exalted it works. You can lock Adamant Skin Technique behind prereqs and it's a balanced purchase with Call the Blade. You can grow forever in Exalted. In this system, like you said, 5-10 Charms, tops. Knowing that, you'll try to fit the best Charms into a tight budget, ignoring the majority of them. So it's a bunch of stuff to sift through, looking for the best gems.<br /> <br /> Sorry, I'm kind of rambling. All I know is that, as written, I would be hard pressed to buy anything besides Adamant Circle Sorcery. Screw taking a Charm to hide my sword or whatever, I can take a Charm to drop meteors, stop time, and turn into a dragon. All as one Charm. I'd take Adamant Sorcery 10 times.<br /> <br /> Seriously, spells can do everything! Teleport, turn invisible, fly, mind control, information gather, buffs, debuffs, battlefield control, summons, heals, blast. I see no reason to take Eagle Wing when I could just cast Fly. No reason for stealth charms with Superior Invisibility around.<br /> <br /> This is from the DnD optimization perspective, which I got big in to. The tier system pretty much states that playing Fighter is almost pointless. It states that spells are more powerful than class features, and Shapechange makes you a better Fighter than the Fighter.<br /> <br /> Your goal is not a solution to tiers, so maybe you're fine with the Dominions fitting square into the tier system. I guess maybe I'm just rambling on my overall dissatisfaction with what I perceive to be an unbearable flaw with 3.5/Pathfinder, and by cramming Exalted into this system I think it suffers for it. Sorry if it seems like I'm thread crapping, that's not the intent. Trying to offer my opinion at the system at a glance. I'll try to be more thoughtful and coherent when it isn't 1am.<br /> <br /> You did replicate the mechanics of every charm (so many!) in creative ways. That itself is commendable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T07:18:26-07:00","id":543884,"title":"","content":"I, personally, am satisfied with the martial class consistant damage vs. evoker burst damage paradigm presented in Pathfinder. The wizard's advantages over a fighter are less significant (though admittedly still present, especially at level 13+) in the grueling war of attrition that is a dungeon crawl, and Pathfinder is <i>about</i> dungeon crawls, not PVP. Balancing the game in Exalted becomes a PVP discussion because even most of the NPC antagonists whom are a threat to the PCs are also built using PC splats.<br /> <br /> My satisfaction with the status quo doesn't exist because I have some kind of bias in favor of wizards; I play rangers and paladins most of the time anyway, which are basically fighters. Though in regards to your &quot;fighters are almost pointless in Pathfinder&quot; assertion, I will admit that <i>rangers</i> can do pretty much everything a fighter can, <i>and</i> get tertiary spell progression, 6 + Int mod skill points per level, and a bunch of useful class features like Favored Enemies and an animal companion on top of it.<br /> <br /> Most stealthy characters in Pathfinder pick up a <i>ring of invisibility </i>eventually anyway. The balancing thing about utility spells is they're easy to imitate with items. Classes that actually have those utility skills as class skills <i>and</i> possess those items have far more utility than a wizard with just the spell.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say, if you find something unbearable in Pathfinder, Mythic rules will just turn it, and everything else, up to 11, and I've tried to balance each Caste like a new Mythic Path as much as possible.<br /> <br /> I could talk <i>all day</i> about this paradigm and why it's balanced enough to give martial characters and spellcasters each a compelling playspace in Pathfinder, but that would derail this thread pretty badly, so I'd prefer not to.<br /> <br /> Additionally, you won't be able to pick the 10 best Dominion Abilities because you can only pick your 1st-Tier Dominion Ability from Dominion Abilities you <i>qualify for</i> at 1st Tier. And you can only select your 2nd Tier Dominion Ability from Dominion Abilities you qualify for at 2nd Tier, and so on.<br /> <br /> In regards to the way Adamant Circle Sorcery works above, you make a good point; I think I may need to nerf it slightly, but keep in mind it's <i>already</i> a less efficient way to cast spells than a Twilight Caste sorcerer/wizard/arcanist using Twilight Arcana (or the Archmage equivalent ability: Wild Magic). Adamant Circle Sorcery is designed more for Solars with high Intelligence scores that <i>don't </i>get arcane spellcasting from their class levels.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-07-2015, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T13:21:26-07:00","id":544213,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The design goal for Adamant Circle Sorcery should be to complement the idea presented in Exalted's lore that Solars were sorcerer-kings regardless of their actual Caste, and could be again. It should be compelling to take when you want access to specific spells, but not overshadow the other Dominion Abilities. This is a feedback thread, so if anyone has some specific math recommendations (number of spells per purchase of the ability, mote cost per spell level) feel free to offer them.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, I'd originally named this Dominion Ability &quot;The Gift of Bridget&quot;. Does anyone think that (or another name) fits more with the ability's design goals?</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-07-2015, 04:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T21:50:32-07:00","id":546468,"title":"","content":"I've been holding off on posting so I can say something more useful than &quot;hut dur tiers&quot; again.<br /> <br /> If you want to extol the virtues of Pathfinder without derailing the thread, I'm happy to listen in a PM. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Brigid&quot; not &quot;Bridget&quot;, right? I feel like Brigid came up with Sorcery but not the Spirit Charms. I feel like Magic Dominion is about right.<br /> <br /> Interesting to hear you're fine with the system as is. I always thought the argument that Fighters have stamina was odd. They have a resource just like everyone else: hit points. And they're usually the worst equipped to get them back, with no access to UMD healing wands. Anyway, about the actual mechanics!<br /> <br /> I think three spells per Charm sounds about right. That should grant an immense amount of power to martial types I had originally discounted as a balance point. No real flexibility though, which is probably the purview of full casters. Honestly, assuming all Solars grab Adamant Sorcery, they can level the tier playing field quite nicely.<br /> <br /> It's very common to include summoning and counter magic as free in house rules. Maybe include Summon Monster 1-9 and the ability to counter spells as a prepared/interrupt action for free and reduce the number to two spells? Or make it &quot;learn your tier in spell levels&quot; so you can learn a bunch of low level spells or one high level one? Just random thoughts.<br /> <br /> I still think a lot of the Charms could use collapsing. Many are pretty boring, or serve as speed bumps to higher tiers. This is also my complaint about Exalted. For example, there is an armor Charm to banish armor and to reduce armor check penalties. Why isn't that just one Charm? &quot;Reduce the penalty. Also, spend a mote to banish armor.&quot; Smaller benefits being folded together would go a long ways to making lower tier Charms compare to higher ones more favorably, especially Sorcery.<br /> <br /> And there are a lot of Charms to &quot;cast x as a spell-like&quot; such as the Spirit Detecting Glance. That also has to be balanced against Sorcery. You can access it earlier with SDG than Sorcery, but Sorcery is cheaper and gives you more spells. Folding SDG in to Spirit Cutting Technique would balance those a bit. I guess I'm just saying &quot;Consider folding prereqs together to improve balance. And careful with spell-likes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe nerf Sorcery to spells of 1/2 tier so as not to muscle in on caster territory? This gives more room to balance spell-likes without it being &quot;just take sorcery.&quot; Though I really like the idea of a Fighter with Shapechange!<br /> <br /> Oh, and you misspelled Rogue as &quot;Rouge&quot; under Flow Like Blood three times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I hope this was more helpful this time around!<br /> <br /> Edit: I keep forgetting that it seems your goal is to balance this with the standard Mythic rules, which I have next to no experience with. If the power level of most Charms seems right, I think the offender is Sorcery. But I usually increase everything to match rather than bring down something awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":4729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","user":"Childofthesun1","date":". 06-09-2015, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T09:36:25-07:00","id":547162,"title":"","content":"If anyone wants to help with balance but doesn't own a copy of <i>Mythic Adventures</i>, remember, Pathfinder is Open Source, so you can find the rules for free on the Paizo SRD: <a href=\"http://paizo.com/pathfinderRPG/prd/mythicAdventures/mythicHeroes.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://paizo.com/pathfinderRPG/prd/m...hicHeroes.html</a><br /> <br /> Or the fan made PFSRD, which is easier to navigate, IMO: <a href=\"http://www.d20pfsrd.com/mythic/mythic-heroes\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.d20pfsrd.com/mythic/mythic-heroes</a><br /> <br /> The things an Exalt can accomplish by spending three motes (in the above build, not in Exalted proper) should be roughly equivalent to what a mythic hero can accomplish with one use of mythic power, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;<br /> &quot;You're in an ancient Solar tomb.&quot;<br /> &quot;I roll Lore (Farming)!&quot;","edited":{"userid":1844,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","user":"Ranger_Lord","date":". 06-09-2015, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1844-ranger_lord","name":"Ranger_Lord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1844_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}